% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GSC: the syntactically-grassroots checker.
%
% Decides def:syntactically-grassroots of /Grassroots/GSC, Section 3, one
% definition for a contract of agent roles and listed roles (GSC ac7ad63),
% with the values of its appendix "Values in Speech-Act Schemas" (app:numbers).
% The signed term, reflexive predicates and contracts with wards are GAI's
% extension of the language (GAI's appendix "Contracts with Wards"; GSC
% 83b951c and 1a2a5f3), held here for GAI.  The papers are the specification
% and no definition of them is restated here; each procedure names the
% definition it decides.  README.md maps the two.
%
% This file is the directory's shared scope: the representation of a contract,
% the substitution and matching machinery every condition needs, and the
% directory's entry points.
%
% The condition on a contract with wards is GAI's (Coordination Appendix B;
% Udi, 2026-10-20) and lives in the child directory wards/, entered through
% its self.glp by the qualifier wards (TGLP, Section "Module System",
% "Cross-module type checking": a qualifier is a child directory or module
% file of the caller's directory).  It reads the introductions of a schema,
% intro_act_bindings/2 of unobstructed.glp, which this file exposes to its
% subtree (TGLP, "The -expose directive").
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-expose(unobstructed).

% --- The syntax of a schema (def:role, def:schema) -------------------------
% A name term (def:role): own(I) is <pi_I>, for an agent role pi_I of its
% schema, and ext(Sigma, Y) is Sigma.y.  own_var(X), <x> for an agent
% variable x, is read and is no name term of def:role: a contract carrying
% one is refused (name_term_base, check.glp).
%
% An atom marked - may have the wildcard * among its arguments, or in place
% of the speech-act variable of a name term among them (def:schema, GSC
% 327e035): any is the wildcard as an argument, and ext_any(Sigma) the name
% term Sigma.*, which def:role admits in a cleared atom (Definition Name
% term, GSC 14c921c; GSN.glp).  Such an atom is a cleared atom, of *(i): it
% deletes every atom of the agent's state that it matches and requires none
% (def:schema, def:binding, def:compile's K_p).  The term form writes it
% among a role's deleted atoms; rs_del below gives -(i), the deleted atoms
% with no wildcard, and rs_clear *(i).
NameTerm  ::= own(Integer) ; own_var(Constant)
            ; ext(NameTerm, Constant) ; ext_any(NameTerm).
NameTerms ::= [] ; [NameTerm | NameTerms].

% An argument is a role, named by its index in the schema, a party variable, a
% speech-act variable, a name term or a signed term: sgn(Y, I) is the signed
% term sgn(y, pi_I) of def:schema, the speech act y signed by the agent in
% role I.  Speech-act schemas allow numbers (GSC, Section 3.2, the paragraph after
% the example of def:schema, and def:numbers): num(X) is a value argument,
% the value variable X where X is a name and the number X where X is a
% number.
Arg   ::= role(Integer) ; pvar(Constant) ; svar(Constant) ; nterm(NameTerm)
        ; sgn(Constant, Integer) ; num(Constant) ; any.
Args  ::= [] ; [Arg | Args].
Atom  ::= atom(Constant, Args).
Atoms ::= [] ; [Atom | Atoms].

% --- The values speech-act schemas allow (GSC, def:numbers) -----------------------
% "Speech-act schemas allow values of any type: an argument of an atom may be a
% value or a value variable, a schema may carry a constraint on its value
% variables, which every binding satisfies, and an atom added or deleted may
% carry a multiplicity, a count of copies and so a positive whole number"
% (Section 3.2; def:numbers and def:binding-numbers in the appendix).  times(K, A) is the
% atom A with the multiplicity K, K a value argument; a constraint is a
% conjunction of linear equalities and inequalities over value arguments
% (Constraint below), extending the term form of Currencies' GB.glp.  A
% schema with a constraint is nschema(Name, Vars, Constraint, Roles), its
% value variables listed in Vars with its other variables, in the order of
% its head.  The contract as written is of the types N...; traceable
% provenance and volition are decided on its plain form, plain_decl below,
% the multiplicities and the constraint dropped and the value arguments
% kept, since "a number names no agent, so the conditions below do not
% concern them" (GSC, ibid.; the appendix, after def:binding-numbers).
% def:unobstructed is decided on the contract as written (unobstructed.glp):
% its clauses ask that an atom be added at a binding, which satisfies its
% schema's constraint (def:binding-numbers), so a number is matched by
% equality under that binding.
Mult       ::= Atom ; times(Arg, Atom).
Mults      ::= [] ; [Mult | Mults].
% A constraint is "a conjunction of linear equalities and inequalities over
% its value variables and values" (def:numbers): true, and(C1, C2), and
% eq, le, lt, ge and gt of two expressions, X = Y, X =< Y, X < Y, X >= Y and
% X > Y, with succ(X, Y), Y = X + 1, as Currencies' GB.glp writes it.  An
% expression is a value argument, plus(X, Y), minus(X, Y) or mul(X, Y), the
% last linear where X or Y has no value variable.  or(C1, C2) is read so
% that a contract carrying it is refused, a disjunction being no conjunction
% (constraint_not_conjunction, check.glp), and so is a product of two
% expressions that each carry a value variable (constraint_not_linear).
% signed(U, Y) and unsigned(U, Y) are the signing conditions signed(u, y) and unsigned(u, y), u an agent role or agent variable and y a speech-act variable of the schema (def:numbers, GSC 10fcc92): U is role(I), I an agent role of the schema, or pvar(X), and Y is svar(Y), each variable listed in the head; any other U is a fault signing_not_agent(Schema, U) and any other Y a fault signing_not_speech_act(Schema, Y) (check.glp).  The conditions of def:syntactically-grassroots read no signing condition (the appendix, after def:binding-numbers), so the checker takes each as true.
Constraint ::= true ; and(Constraint, Constraint)
             ; eq(Expr, Expr) ; le(Expr, Expr) ; lt(Expr, Expr)
             ; ge(Expr, Expr) ; gt(Expr, Expr) ; succ(Arg, Arg)
             ; or(Constraint, Constraint)
             ; signed(Arg, Arg) ; unsigned(Arg, Arg).
Expr       ::= Arg ; plus(Expr, Expr) ; minus(Expr, Expr) ; mul(Expr, Expr).
Exprs      ::= [] ; [Expr | Exprs].
% A schema's constraint, and the value variables it uses as multiplicities,
% which a binding sends to positive whole numbers (def:binding-numbers).
NumCtx     ::= nc(Constraint, Args).

% The base of an argument, of a name term and of a role (def:role,
% def:grounded).
% A value argument names no agent, and its base, b_num, is the base of no
% role (GSC, Section 3.2); prov.glp and volition.glp pass it by.
% The wildcard is no agent role, variable or name term, and has no base
% either (def:grounded, def:schema), b_any; it occurs only in a cleared
% atom, which no condition reads.
Base  ::= b_role(Integer) ; b_pvar(Constant) ; b_svar(Constant) ; b_num ; b_any.
Bases ::= [] ; [Base | Bases].

% rs(Guard, Add, Del, Keep, Forb) holds an agent role's four multisets in the
% order +(i), -(i), =(i), not(i); Guard records the mark ?, which only an
% agent role may carry (def:schema).  crs(Kind, Guard, Add, Del, Keep, Forb)
% is the same for a listed role (def:role): listed(I, Rho, Args) is the
% listed role pi_I[rho(*, u_2, ..., u_r)] of the agent role pi_I, Args its
% arguments u_2, ..., u_r (GSC 8064cfb); its Guard is unguarded, and a listed
% role carrying ? is refused (listed_guarded).
Guard     ::= guarded ; unguarded.
RoleKind  ::= listed(Integer, Constant, Args).
RoleSpec  ::= rs(Guard, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms)
            ; crs(RoleKind, Guard, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms).
RoleSpecs ::= [] ; [RoleSpec | RoleSpecs].

% A schema with a listed role may be written cschema(Name, Vars, [], Roles),
% as the owners' contracts write close: its third argument is the empty
% list, where reach conditions stood until GSC f3c4f43 removed them.  A
% schema's second argument is its variables, pvar(X) and svar(Y), in the
% order of its head (def:schema, GSC 0228e79).
Nil       ::= [].
Schema    ::= schema(Constant, Args, RoleSpecs)
            ; cschema(Constant, Args, Nil, RoleSpecs).
Contract  ::= [] ; [Schema | Contract].

% A contract may declare predicates of arity one reflexive (GAI's appendix
% "Contracts with Wards", "Reflexive predicates"); one that does is written
% reflexive(Preds, Schemas), and one that does not is the list of its
% schemas.
Declared  ::= Contract ; reflexive(Preds, Contract).

% The contract as written, with the values speech-act schemas allow: a role's four
% multisets may carry multiplicities, which def:numbers admits on an atom
% added, deleted or required and check.glp refuses on one forbidden
% (multiplicity_forbidden), and a schema may be written nschema, with a
% constraint.  A contract with no
% number is of these types as it is of the plain ones.
NRoleSpec  ::= rs(Guard, Mults, Mults, Mults, Mults)
             ; crs(RoleKind, Guard, Mults, Mults, Mults, Mults).
NRoleSpecs ::= [] ; [NRoleSpec | NRoleSpecs].
NSchema    ::= schema(Constant, Args, NRoleSpecs)
             ; cschema(Constant, Args, Nil, NRoleSpecs)
             ; nschema(Constant, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs).
NContract  ::= [] ; [NSchema | NContract].
NDeclared  ::= NContract ; reflexive(Preds, NContract).

% The contract as its owner writes it (GSC 25b6b3c, Section 2: "A name in a
% pragma is the schema's role of that name, the schemas naming their roles as
% the clauses do"; GKK.glp, GSG.glp and GSN.glp at GLP ec7c578c): a schema's
% head lists its roles by the clause's names, schema(Name, Names, Vars,
% Roles), cschema(Name, Names, Vars, [], Roles) and nschema(Name, Names, Vars,
% Constraint, Roles), Names the names of its roles in order, a listed role
% named by its base; a schema written without them, as the owners' contracts
% not yet rewritten write it, is read as before.  A contract may name its
% environment predicates (GSC 25b6b3c, Section 3.2 and the appendix "Values
% in Speech-Act Schemas": "whose atoms are over values, which the machine holds from
% startup and the platform keeps current, and which no schema adds or
% deletes"), environment(Preds, Body), Body the contract with or without its
% reflexive predicates.  The checker, the compiler to VMAT and the printer
% read it through unnamed/2, which drops the names and the environment
% predicates, and env_preds/2, which gives the environment predicates; the
% printer prints each role by its name (notation.glp).
% A name in the head is a role's name, or one(Name, Other), the role Name
% possibly the person of the role Other (GSC 316d875, Section 2: "a clause
% that admits one person in both writes 'Alice and Bob, possibly one
% person'; the schema's head writes the second name as one('Bob', 'Alice')").
RName     ::= Constant ; one(Constant, Constant).
Names      ::= [] ; [RName | Names].
RChunks     ::= [] ; [RName | RChunks].
% The clause syntax (GSC 859a007, Sections 3.1 and 3.2, Definitions Name
% term, role, Speech-act schema and Schema with values), as GSC #11 Cowork
% settled its term (Code inbox, 2026-11-04 19:57 UTC and 2026-11-05 06:28
% UTC): sas(Name, Names, Vars, Head, Body, Constraint, Guards), the schema
% tau: H <- B, gamma guarded by G.  Names is every person of the schema in
% order --- its roles, its listed-role variables and its agent variables ---
% a name holding a literal being an agent role (def:role), written
% one(Name, Other) where its clause admits the two as one person; Vars is
% every variable of the schema that is no role, its agent variables, its
% speech-act variables and its value variables (def:schema, "its variables";
% def:numbers); Head and Body are its literals, an atom atom(Pred,
% [Holder|Args]) or not(Atom), and its quantified conjuncts forall(X, Cond,
% Lits), X the listed role, Cond the atom rho(pi, X, u_2, ..., u_r) at its
% base and Lits the literals with holder X (def:role); a multiplicity is
% times(K, Atom) (def:numbers); Constraint is gamma, true where the schema
% has none; Guards the names of its guarding roles.  An argument is a name
% or a variable of Vars, a constant either way, own(Name) for <Name>,
% ext(Sigma, Y) for Sigma.y, the wildcard the constant '_' and
% ext(Sigma, '_') for Sigma._, a value num(X), and a signed term sgn(Y,
% Name).  A constant is read by =?= against Names and Vars, and its
% constant taken from there (sas_bare below).
SNT    ::= own(Constant) ; ext(SNT, Constant).
SArg   ::= Constant ; own(Constant) ; ext(SNT, Constant) ; num(Constant)
         ; sgn(Constant, Constant).
SArgs  ::= [] ; [SArg | SArgs].
SAtom  ::= atom(Constant, SArgs).
SAtoms ::= [] ; [SAtom | SAtoms].
SMult  ::= SAtom ; times(SArg, SAtom).
SQLit  ::= SMult ; not(SMult).
SQLits ::= [] ; [SQLit | SQLits].
SLit   ::= SQLit ; forall(Constant, SAtom, SQLits).
SLits  ::= [] ; [SLit | SLits].
SExpr  ::= SArg ; plus(SExpr, SExpr) ; minus(SExpr, SExpr) ; mul(SExpr, SExpr).
SConstraint ::= true ; and(SConstraint, SConstraint)
              ; eq(SExpr, SExpr) ; le(SExpr, SExpr) ; lt(SExpr, SExpr)
              ; ge(SExpr, SExpr) ; gt(SExpr, SExpr) ; succ(SArg, SArg)
              ; or(SConstraint, SConstraint)
              ; signed(SArg, SArg) ; unsigned(SArg, SArg).
PNames ::= [] ; [Constant | PNames].
WSchema    ::= schema(Constant, Args, NRoleSpecs)
             ; cschema(Constant, Args, Nil, NRoleSpecs)
             ; nschema(Constant, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs)
             ; schema(Constant, Names, Args, NRoleSpecs)
             ; cschema(Constant, Names, Args, Nil, NRoleSpecs)
             ; nschema(Constant, Names, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs)
             ; sas(Constant, Names, PNames, SLits, SLits, SConstraint, PNames).
WContract  ::= [] ; [WSchema | WContract].
WBody      ::= WContract ; reflexive(Preds, WContract).
WDeclared  ::= WBody ; environment(Preds, WBody).

% The contract as the checker reads it, its names and environment predicates
% dropped.
procedure unnamed(WDeclared?, NDeclared).
unnamed([], []).
unnamed([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c([S?|Ss?], C).
unnamed(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c(Ss?, C).
unnamed(environment(_, B), D?) :- ground(B?) | unnamed_b(B?, D).
procedure unnamed_b(WBody?, NDeclared).
unnamed_b([], []).
unnamed_b([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c([S?|Ss?], C).
unnamed_b(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c(Ss?, C).
procedure unnamed_c(WContract?, NContract).
unnamed_c([], []).
unnamed_c([S|Ss], [S1?|Ss1?]) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    unnamed_s(S?, S1),
    unnamed_c(Ss?, Ss1).
procedure unnamed_s(WSchema?, NSchema).
unnamed_s(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(cschema(Nm, Vs, X, Rs), cschema(Nm?, Vs?, X?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(nschema(Nm, Vs, Cn, Rs), nschema(Nm?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(schema(Nm, _, Vs, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(cschema(Nm, _, Vs, X, Rs), cschema(Nm?, Vs?, X?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(nschema(Nm, _, Vs, Cn, Rs), nschema(Nm?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(sas(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G), S?) :-
    ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?), ground(Vs?), ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?), ground(G?) |
    sas_schema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, H?, B?, Cn?, G?, S).
% The names of a schema's roles in order, for the printer (notation.glp):
% nm(Name) for a role its schema names, dflt for one it does not --- each
% role of a schema written without names, and a listed role of one written
% schema(Name, Names, Vars, Roles), which names it by its base.
NameOf  ::= nm(RName) ; dflt.
NameOfs ::= [] ; [NameOf | NameOfs].
procedure wsch_rnames(WSchema?, NameOfs).
wsch_rnames(schema(_, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(nschema(_, _, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(schema(_, Ns, _, Rs), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(cschema(_, Ns, _, _, Rs), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(nschema(_, Ns, _, _, Rs), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(sas(_, Ns, _, H, B, _, _), R?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(H?), ground(B?) |
    sas_split(H?, HP, HQ),
    sas_split(B?, BP, BQ),
    sas_qapp(HP?, BP?, PP),
    sas_quapp(HQ?, BQ?, QQ),
    sas_table(Ns?, PP?, QQ?, 1, E),
    sas_rnames(E?, R).
procedure old_rnames(Names?, NRoleSpecs?, NameOfs).
old_rnames(_, [], []).
old_rnames([], [_|Rs], [dflt|R?]) :- old_rnames([], Rs?, R).
old_rnames([N|Ns], [rs(_, _, _, _, _)|Rs], [nm(N?)|R?]) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
old_rnames([_|Ns], [crs(_, _, _, _, _, _)|Rs], [dflt|R?]) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
% The environment predicates a contract names, [] where it names none.
procedure env_preds(WDeclared?, Preds).
env_preds([], []).
env_preds([_|_], []).
env_preds(reflexive(_, _), []).
env_preds(environment(Ps, _), Ps?).

% --- Reading the clause syntax (GSC 859a007, def:role, def:schema, def:numbers)
% sas_schema reads sas(Name, Names, Vars, Head, Body, Constraint, Guards)
% into the form the checker decides.  Its roles are numbered in the order of
% Names: a name that is the holder of a literal of Head or Body outside its
% quantified conjuncts is an agent role (def:role: "An agent role of a
% schema is an agent variable that is the holder of a literal of it"), a
% name a quantified conjunct quantifies a listed role, and any other an
% agent variable.  An agent role pi_i has +(i) the atoms of Head with holder
% pi_i, -(i) and the cleared atoms _(i) those negated there, =(i) the atoms
% of Body with holder pi_i and not(i) those negated there; a listed role
% reads the same off the literals of its conjuncts in Head and in Body, and
% its kind pi[rho(_, u_2, ..., u_r)] off their condition (def:schema: "a
% listed role requires and forbids by the literals of its conjunct in B,
% adds, deletes and clears by those of its conjunct in H, and requires
% besides the atom its quantifier is conditioned on, held by its base"; the
% checker's form carries that atom as the role's kind).  Definition
% Speech-act schema requires -(i) a subset of =(i), and the checker's form
% holds =(i) less -(i), its role requiring the two together (nrs_req), so
% Keep is =(i) less -(i), a copy for each copy deleted (sas_minus).  Each
% atom is written without its holder (def:schema: "Each such atom is
% written without its holder").  The variables of the checker's form are
% Vars in order, an agent variable pvar(X), a value variable --- one the
% schema writes num(X) --- num(X), and any other svar(X).

% Whether a constant is the name N, one(N, Other) being N.
procedure(X) sas_nameq(X?, RName?, Ans).
sas_nameq(X, one(M, _), yes) :- X? =?= M? | true.
sas_nameq(X, M, yes) :- otherwise, X? =?= M? | true.
sas_nameq(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure(X) sas_in_names(X?, Names?, Ans).
sas_in_names(_, [], no).
sas_in_names(X, [N|Ns], R?) :- ground(X?), ground(N?), ground(Ns?) |
    sas_nameq(X?, N?, A),
    sas_in_names1(A?, X?, Ns?, R).

procedure(X) sas_in_names1(Ans?, X?, Names?, Ans).
sas_in_names1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_in_names1(no, X, Ns, R?) :- sas_in_names(X?, Ns?, R).

% A variable of Vars, by =?=, and its constant.
VFound ::= vfound(Constant) ; vnone.
procedure(X) sas_var(X?, PNames?, VFound).
sas_var(_, [], vnone).
sas_var(X, [V|_], vfound(V?)) :- X? =?= V? | true.
sas_var(X, [_|Vs], R?) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | sas_var(X?, Vs?, R).

procedure sas_in(Constant?, PNames?, Ans).
sas_in(_, [], no).
sas_in(X, [Y|_], yes) :- X? =?= Y? | true.
sas_in(X, [_|Ys], R?) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | sas_in(X?, Ys?, R).

procedure sas_qapp(SQLits?, SQLits?, SQLits).
sas_qapp([], T, T?).
sas_qapp([L|Ls], T, [L?|R?]) :- sas_qapp(Ls?, T?, R).

procedure sas_aapp(SAtoms?, SAtoms?, SAtoms).
sas_aapp([], T, T?).
sas_aapp([A|As], T, [A?|R?]) :- sas_aapp(As?, T?, R).

% The literals of a list, and its quantified conjuncts q(X, Cond, Lits).
Quant  ::= q(Constant, SAtom, SQLits).
Quants ::= [] ; [Quant | Quants].
procedure sas_quapp(Quants?, Quants?, Quants).
sas_quapp([], T, T?).
sas_quapp([Q|Qs], T, [Q?|R?]) :- sas_quapp(Qs?, T?, R).

procedure sas_split(SLits?, SQLits, Quants).
sas_split([], [], []).
sas_split([forall(X, C, Q)|Ls], P?, [q(X?, C?, Q?)|R?]) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, R).
sas_split([not(M)|Ls], [not(M?)|P?], R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, R).
sas_split([atom(F, As)|Ls], [atom(F?, As?)|P?], R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, R).
sas_split([times(K, A)|Ls], [times(K?, A?)|P?], R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, R).

% A literal's atom, its multiplicity and whether it is negated.
procedure sas_lit_atom(SQLit?, SAtom).
sas_lit_atom(atom(F, As), atom(F?, As?)).
sas_lit_atom(times(_, A), A?).
sas_lit_atom(not(atom(F, As)), atom(F?, As?)).
sas_lit_atom(not(times(_, A)), A?).

procedure sas_lit_mult(SQLit?, SMult).
sas_lit_mult(atom(F, As), atom(F?, As?)).
sas_lit_mult(times(K, A), times(K?, A?)).
sas_lit_mult(not(M), M?).

procedure sas_lit_neg(SQLit?, Ans).
sas_lit_neg(not(_), yes).
sas_lit_neg(atom(_, _), no).
sas_lit_neg(times(_, _), no).

procedure sas_pred(SAtom?, Constant).
sas_pred(atom(P, _), P?).

% Whether the name N is the holder of an atom.
procedure sas_atom_held(SAtom?, RName?, Ans).
sas_atom_held(atom(_, []), _, no).
sas_atom_held(atom(_, [H|_]), N, R?) :- sas_nameq(H?, N?, R).

procedure sas_lit_held(SQLit?, RName?, Ans).
sas_lit_held(L, N, R?) :- ground(L?) |
    sas_lit_atom(L?, A),
    sas_atom_held(A?, N?, R).

% Whether N holds some literal of a list, and whether some conjunct
% quantifies it.
procedure sas_holds(SQLits?, RName?, Ans).
sas_holds([], _, no).
sas_holds([L|Ls], N, R?) :- ground(Ls?), ground(N?) |
    sas_lit_held(L?, N?, A),
    sas_holds1(A?, Ls?, N?, R).

procedure sas_holds1(Ans?, SQLits?, RName?, Ans).
sas_holds1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_holds1(no, Ls, N, R?) :- sas_holds(Ls?, N?, R).

procedure sas_quant(Quants?, RName?, Ans).
sas_quant([], _, no).
sas_quant([q(X, _, _)|Qs], N, R?) :- ground(Qs?), ground(N?) |
    sas_nameq(X?, N?, A),
    sas_quant1(A?, Qs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_quant1(Ans?, Quants?, RName?, Ans).
sas_quant1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_quant1(no, Qs, N, R?) :- sas_quant(Qs?, N?, R).

% The roles of a schema, numbered in the order of its names: ar(Name, I) an
% agent role, lr(Name, I) a listed role and av(Name) an agent variable.
REnt  ::= ar(RName, Integer) ; lr(RName, Integer) ; av(RName).
REnts ::= [] ; [REnt | REnts].

procedure sas_table(Names?, SQLits?, Quants?, Integer?, REnts).
sas_table([], _, _, _, []).
sas_table([N|Ns], PP, QQ, I, R?) :-
    ground(N?), ground(Ns?), ground(PP?), ground(QQ?), integer(I?) |
    sas_holds(PP?, N?, A),
    sas_quant(QQ?, N?, Q),
    sas_table1(A?, Q?, N?, Ns?, PP?, QQ?, I?, R).

procedure sas_table1(Ans?, Ans?, RName?, Names?, SQLits?, Quants?, Integer?, REnts).
sas_table1(yes, _, N, Ns, PP, QQ, I, [ar(N?, I?)|R?]) :- integer(I?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    sas_table(Ns?, PP?, QQ?, I1?, R).
sas_table1(no, yes, N, Ns, PP, QQ, I, [lr(N?, I?)|R?]) :- integer(I?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    sas_table(Ns?, PP?, QQ?, I1?, R).
sas_table1(no, no, N, Ns, PP, QQ, I, [av(N?)|R?]) :- sas_table(Ns?, PP?, QQ?, I?, R).

% The names of the roles, for the printer (wsch_rnames).
procedure sas_rnames(REnts?, NameOfs).
sas_rnames([], []).
sas_rnames([ar(N, _)|Es], [nm(N?)|R?]) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).
sas_rnames([lr(N, _)|Es], [nm(N?)|R?]) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).
sas_rnames([av(_)|Es], R?) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).

Look ::= lrole(Integer) ; lvar ; lnone.
procedure(X) sas_look(X?, REnts?, Look).
sas_look(_, [], lnone).
sas_look(N, [ar(M, I)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lrole(I?), N?, Es?, R).
sas_look(N, [lr(M, I)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lrole(I?), N?, Es?, R).
sas_look(N, [av(M)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lvar, N?, Es?, R).

procedure(X) sas_look1(Ans?, Look?, X?, REnts?, Look).
sas_look1(yes, L, _, _, L?).
sas_look1(no, _, N, Es, R?) :- sas_look(N?, Es?, R).

procedure sas_index(Look?, Integer).
sas_index(lrole(I), I?).
sas_index(lvar, 0).
sas_index(lnone, 0).

% An argument (def:role, def:schema, def:numbers).  A constant is the
% wildcard, a role, an agent variable or another variable of Vars; one that
% is none of these is a fault of the reading, not_in_vars (sas_faults), and
% is read as the wildcard, which no condition reads.
procedure sas_arg(SArg?, REnts?, PNames?, Arg).
sas_arg(own(N), E, _, nterm(R?)) :- sas_nt(own(N?), E?, R).
sas_arg(ext(S, Y), E, _, nterm(R?)) :- sas_nt(ext(S?, Y?), E?, R).
sas_arg(num(X), _, _, num(X?)).
sas_arg(sgn(Y, N), E, _, sgn(Y?, I?)) :-
    sas_look(N?, E?, L),
    sas_index(L?, I).
sas_arg(C, E, V, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare(C?, E?, V?, R).

procedure(X) sas_bare(X?, REnts?, PNames?, Arg).
sas_bare(C, _, _, any) :- C? =?= '_' | true.
sas_bare(C, E, V, R?) :- otherwise, ground(C?) |
    sas_look(C?, E?, L),
    sas_var(C?, V?, F),
    sas_bare1(L?, F?, R).

procedure sas_bare1(Look?, VFound?, Arg).
sas_bare1(lrole(I), _, role(I?)).
sas_bare1(lvar, vfound(X), pvar(X?)).
sas_bare1(lnone, vfound(X), svar(X?)).
sas_bare1(lvar, vnone, any).
sas_bare1(lnone, vnone, any).

procedure sas_nt(SNT?, REnts?, NameTerm).
sas_nt(own(N), E, R?) :- ground(N?) |
    sas_look(N?, E?, L),
    sas_own(L?, N?, R).
sas_nt(ext(S, Y), E, ext_any(R?)) :- Y? =?= '_' | sas_nt(S?, E?, R).
sas_nt(ext(S, Y), E, ext(R?, Y?)) :- otherwise | sas_nt(S?, E?, R).

procedure sas_own(Look?, Constant?, NameTerm).
sas_own(lrole(I), _, own(I?)).
sas_own(lvar, N, own_var(N?)).
sas_own(lnone, N, own_var(N?)).

procedure sas_args(SArgs?, REnts?, PNames?, Args).
sas_args([], _, _, []).
sas_args([A|As], E, V, [B?|Bs?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(A?, E?, V?, B),
    sas_args(As?, E?, V?, Bs).

% An atom with its holder dropped, and a multiplicity.
procedure sas_iatom(SAtom?, REnts?, PNames?, Atom).
sas_iatom(atom(P, [_|As]), E, V, atom(P?, R?)) :- sas_args(As?, E?, V?, R).
sas_iatom(atom(P, []), _, _, atom(P?, [])).

procedure sas_imult(SMult?, REnts?, PNames?, Mult).
sas_imult(atom(P, As), E, V, R?) :- sas_iatom(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, R).
sas_imult(times(K, A), E, V, times(K1?, A1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(K?, E?, V?, K1),
    sas_iatom(A?, E?, V?, A1).

% The constraint (def:numbers), its arguments read as an atom's are.
procedure sas_cons(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Constraint).
sas_cons(true, _, _, true).
sas_cons(and(A, B), E, V, and(A1?, B1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_cons(A?, E?, V?, A1), sas_cons(B?, E?, V?, B1).
sas_cons(or(A, B), E, V, or(A1?, B1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_cons(A?, E?, V?, A1), sas_cons(B?, E?, V?, B1).
sas_cons(eq(X, Y), E, V, eq(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(le(X, Y), E, V, le(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(lt(X, Y), E, V, lt(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(ge(X, Y), E, V, ge(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(gt(X, Y), E, V, gt(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(succ(X, Y), E, V, succ(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_arg(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(signed(X, Y), E, V, signed(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_arg(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(unsigned(X, Y), E, V, unsigned(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_arg(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).

procedure sas_expr(SExpr?, REnts?, PNames?, Expr).
sas_expr(plus(X, Y), E, V, plus(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_expr(minus(X, Y), E, V, minus(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_expr(mul(X, Y), E, V, mul(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_expr(own(N), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(own(N?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(ext(S, Y), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(ext(S?, Y?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(num(X), _, _, num(X?)).
sas_expr(sgn(Y, N), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(sgn(Y?, N?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(C, E, V, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare(C?, E?, V?, R).

% The value variables a schema writes, num(X) for X no number.
procedure sas_nums_arg(SArg?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_arg(num(X), T, [X?|T?]).
sas_nums_arg(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_nums_args(SArgs?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_args([], T, T?).
sas_nums_args([A|As], T, R?) :- sas_nums_args(As?, T?, R1), sas_nums_arg(A?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_nums_atom(SAtom?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_atom(atom(_, As), T, R?) :- sas_nums_args(As?, T?, R).

procedure sas_nums_lits(SQLits?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_lits([], T, T?).
sas_nums_lits([L|Ls], T, R?) :- ground(L?) |
    sas_lit_mult(L?, M),
    sas_nums_lits(Ls?, T?, R1),
    sas_nums_mult(M?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_nums_mult(SMult?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_mult(atom(P, As), T, R?) :- sas_nums_atom(atom(P?, As?), T?, R).
sas_nums_mult(times(K, A), T, R?) :- sas_nums_atom(A?, T?, R1), sas_nums_arg(K?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_nums_quants(Quants?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_quants([], T, T?).
sas_nums_quants([q(_, C, Q)|Qs], T, R?) :-
    sas_nums_quants(Qs?, T?, R1),
    sas_nums_lits(Q?, R1?, R2),
    sas_nums_atom(C?, R2?, R).

procedure sas_nums_cons(SConstraint?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_cons(true, T, T?).
sas_nums_cons(and(A, B), T, R?) :- sas_nums_cons(B?, T?, R1), sas_nums_cons(A?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(or(A, B), T, R?) :- sas_nums_cons(B?, T?, R1), sas_nums_cons(A?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(le(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(lt(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(ge(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(gt(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(succ(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_arg(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_arg(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(signed(_, _), T, T?).
sas_nums_cons(unsigned(_, _), T, T?).

procedure sas_nums_expr(SExpr?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_expr(plus(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_expr(minus(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_expr(mul(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_expr(num(X), T, [X?|T?]).
sas_nums_expr(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

% The variables of the checker's form, Vars in order.
procedure sas_vars(PNames?, REnts?, PNames?, Args).
sas_vars([], _, _, []).
sas_vars([X|Xs], E, Ns, [A?|R?]) :- ground(X?), ground(E?), ground(Ns?) |
    sas_look(X?, E?, L),
    sas_in(X?, Ns?, N),
    sas_var_arg(L?, N?, X?, A),
    sas_vars(Xs?, E?, Ns?, R).

procedure sas_var_arg(Look?, Ans?, Constant?, Arg).
sas_var_arg(lrole(I), _, _, role(I?)).
sas_var_arg(lvar, _, X, pvar(X?)).
sas_var_arg(lnone, yes, X, num(X?)).
sas_var_arg(lnone, no, X, svar(X?)).

% The literals of a list with holder N, the atoms and the negated ones, in
% order, each without its holder.
procedure sas_part(SQLits?, RName?, REnts?, PNames?, Mults, Mults).
sas_part([], _, _, _, [], []).
sas_part([L|Ls], N, E, V, P?, Q?) :- ground(L?), ground(N?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_lit_held(L?, N?, A),
    sas_lit_neg(L?, G),
    sas_lit_mult(L?, M),
    sas_part1(A?, G?, M?, Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).

procedure sas_part1(Ans?, Ans?, SMult?, SQLits?, RName?, REnts?, PNames?, Mults, Mults).
sas_part1(yes, no, M, Ls, N, E, V, [X?|P?], Q?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_imult(M?, E?, V?, X),
    sas_part(Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).
sas_part1(yes, yes, M, Ls, N, E, V, P?, [X?|Q?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_imult(M?, E?, V?, X),
    sas_part(Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).
sas_part1(no, _, _, Ls, N, E, V, P?, Q?) :- sas_part(Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).

% The literals and the conditions of the conjuncts over the name N.
procedure sas_qlits(Quants?, RName?, SQLits).
sas_qlits([], _, []).
sas_qlits([q(X, _, Q)|Qs], N, R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Qs?) |
    sas_nameq(X?, N?, A),
    sas_qlits1(A?, Q?, Qs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_qlits1(Ans?, SQLits?, Quants?, RName?, SQLits).
sas_qlits1(yes, Q, Qs, N, R?) :- sas_qlits(Qs?, N?, R1), sas_qapp(Q?, R1?, R).
sas_qlits1(no, _, Qs, N, R?) :- sas_qlits(Qs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_conds(Quants?, RName?, SAtoms).
sas_conds([], _, []).
sas_conds([q(X, C, _)|Qs], N, R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Qs?) |
    sas_nameq(X?, N?, A),
    sas_conds1(A?, C?, Qs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_conds1(Ans?, SAtom?, Quants?, RName?, SAtoms).
sas_conds1(yes, C, Qs, N, [C?|R?]) :- sas_conds(Qs?, N?, R).
sas_conds1(no, _, Qs, N, R?) :- sas_conds(Qs?, N?, R).

% =(i) less -(i), a copy for each copy deleted, and the atoms deleted that
% =(i) does not hold: an atom required k times and deleted j < k times,
% k and j numbers, leaves k - j copies (def:numbers: "kappa copies of
% phi").
Count ::= cnt(Constant, Atom) ; nocnt.
procedure sas_count(Mult?, Count).
sas_count(atom(P, As), cnt(1, atom(P?, As?))).
sas_count(times(num(K), A), cnt(K?, A?)) :- number(K?) | true.
sas_count(_, nocnt) :- otherwise | true.

Cut ::= cut(Mults) ; nocut.
procedure sas_cut(Count?, Count?, Cut).
sas_cut(cnt(K, A), cnt(J, B), cut(R?)) :- A? =?= B?, number(K?), number(J?), K? > J?, ground(A?) |
    N := K? - J?,
    sas_copies(N?, A?, R).
sas_cut(_, _, nocut) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_copies(Constant?, Atom?, Mults).
sas_copies(N, A, [A?]) :- N? =:= 1 | true.
sas_copies(N, A, [times(num(N?), A?)]) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_take(Mults?, Mult?, Mults, Ans).
sas_take([], _, [], no).
sas_take([X|Xs], D, Xs?, yes) :- X? =?= D? | true.
sas_take([X|Xs], D, R?, A?) :- otherwise, ground(X?), ground(D?) |
    sas_count(X?, CX),
    sas_count(D?, CD),
    sas_cut(CX?, CD?, C),
    sas_take1(C?, X?, Xs?, D?, R, A).

procedure sas_take1(Cut?, Mult?, Mults?, Mult?, Mults, Ans).
sas_take1(cut(Ys), _, Xs, _, R?, yes) :- mults_app(Ys?, Xs?, R).
sas_take1(nocut, X, Xs, D, [X?|R?], A?) :- sas_take(Xs?, D?, R, A).

procedure sas_minus(Mults?, Mults?, Mults, Mults).
sas_minus(Rq, [], Rq?, []).
sas_minus(Rq, [D|Ds], K?, M?) :- ground(D?) |
    sas_take(Rq?, D?, Rq1, A),
    sas_minus1(A?, D?, Rq1?, Ds?, K, M).

procedure sas_minus1(Ans?, Mult?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults, Mults).
sas_minus1(yes, _, Rq, Ds, K?, M?) :- sas_minus(Rq?, Ds?, K, M).
sas_minus1(no, D, Rq, Ds, K?, [D?|M?]) :- sas_minus(Rq?, Ds?, K, M).

procedure sas_guard(Ans?, Guard).
sas_guard(yes, guarded).
sas_guard(no, unguarded).

procedure sas_ing(PNames?, RName?, Ans).
sas_ing([], _, no).
sas_ing([G|Gs], N, R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Gs?) |
    sas_nameq(G?, N?, A),
    sas_ing1(A?, Gs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_ing1(Ans?, PNames?, RName?, Ans).
sas_ing1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_ing1(no, Gs, N, R?) :- sas_ing(Gs?, N?, R).

% What a schema is read against: its plain literals and its conjuncts in
% Head and in Body, its guards, its role table and its Vars.
SCtx ::= sctx(SQLits, Quants, SQLits, Quants, PNames, REnts, PNames).

% An agent role N: what it adds and deletes, and requires and forbids.
procedure sas_rs(RName?, SCtx?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_rs(N, sctx(HP, _, BP, _, G, E, V), R?, M?) :- ground(N?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_ing(G?, N?, Gi),
    sas_guard(Gi?, Gd),
    sas_part(HP?, N?, E?, V?, Add, Del),
    sas_part(BP?, N?, E?, V?, Req, Forb),
    sas_rs1(Gd?, Add?, Del?, Req?, Forb?, R, M).

% The role, and the atoms it deletes that it does not require.
procedure sas_rs1(Guard?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_rs1(Gd, Add, Del, Req, Forb, rs(Gd?, Add?, Del?, Keep?, Forb?), M?) :- ground(Del?) |
    mults_cleared(Del?, no, D0),
    sas_minus(Req?, D0?, Keep, M).

% A listed role N, its kind read off its condition.
procedure sas_crs(RName?, SCtx?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_crs(N, sctx(_, HQ, _, BQ, G, E, V), R?, M?) :- ground(N?), ground(HQ?), ground(BQ?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_ing(G?, N?, Gi),
    sas_guard(Gi?, Gd),
    sas_qlits(HQ?, N?, HL),
    sas_qlits(BQ?, N?, BL),
    sas_part(HL?, N?, E?, V?, Add, Del),
    sas_part(BL?, N?, E?, V?, Req, Forb),
    sas_conds(HQ?, N?, C1),
    sas_conds(BQ?, N?, C2),
    sas_aapp(C1?, C2?, Cs),
    sas_kind(Cs?, E?, V?, K),
    sas_crs1(K?, Gd?, Add?, Del?, Req?, Forb?, R, M).

procedure sas_crs1(RoleKind?, Guard?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_crs1(K, Gd, Add, Del, Req, Forb, crs(K?, Gd?, Add?, Del?, Keep?, Forb?), M?) :- ground(Del?) |
    mults_cleared(Del?, no, D0),
    sas_minus(Req?, D0?, Keep, M).

% The kind of a listed role, pi[rho(_, u_2, ..., u_r)], from its condition
% rho(pi, x, u_2, ..., u_r) (def:role); a condition formed otherwise is a
% fault of the reading (quantified_condition), and gives a kind whose base,
% 0, is no agent role.
procedure sas_kind(SAtoms?, REnts?, PNames?, RoleKind).
sas_kind([atom(Rho, [P, _|Us])|_], E, V, listed(I?, Rho?, Us1?)) :- ground(E?) |
    sas_look(P?, E?, L),
    sas_index(L?, I),
    sas_args(Us?, E?, V?, Us1).
sas_kind(_, _, _, listed(0, none, [])) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_roles(REnts?, SCtx?, NRoleSpecs).
sas_roles([], _, []).
sas_roles([ar(N, _)|Ts], C, [RS?|R?]) :- ground(C?) |
    sas_rs(N?, C?, RS, _),
    sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).
sas_roles([lr(N, _)|Ts], C, [RS?|R?]) :- ground(C?) |
    sas_crs(N?, C?, RS, _),
    sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).
sas_roles([av(_)|Ts], C, R?) :- sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).

procedure sas_has_lr(REnts?, Ans).
sas_has_lr([], no).
sas_has_lr([lr(_, _)|_], yes).
sas_has_lr([ar(_, _)|Ts], R?) :- sas_has_lr(Ts?, R).
sas_has_lr([av(_)|Ts], R?) :- sas_has_lr(Ts?, R).

procedure sas_true(SConstraint?, Ans).
sas_true(true, yes).
sas_true(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_schema(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, PNames?, NSchema).
sas_schema(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G, S?) :-
    sas_split(H?, HP, HQ),
    sas_split(B?, BP, BQ),
    sas_schema0(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, Cn?, G?, S).

procedure sas_schema0(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SQLits?, Quants?, SQLits?, Quants?, SConstraint?, PNames?, NSchema).
sas_schema0(Nm, Ns, Vs, HP, HQ, BP, BQ, Cn, G, S?) :-
    ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?) |
    sas_qapp(HP?, BP?, PP),
    sas_quapp(HQ?, BQ?, QQ),
    sas_table(Ns?, PP?, QQ?, 1, E),
    sas_schema1(Nm?, sctx(HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, G?, E?, Vs?), Cn?, S).

procedure sas_schema1(Constant?, SCtx?, SConstraint?, NSchema).
sas_schema1(Nm, sctx(HP, HQ, BP, BQ, G, E, Vs), Cn, S?) :-
    ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?), ground(Cn?) |
    sas_roles(E?, sctx(HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, G?, E?, Vs?), Rs),
    sas_has_lr(E?, L),
    sas_true(Cn?, T),
    sas_nums_lits(HP?, [], N1),
    sas_nums_lits(BP?, N1?, N2),
    sas_nums_quants(HQ?, N2?, N3),
    sas_nums_quants(BQ?, N3?, N4),
    sas_nums_cons(Cn?, N4?, Nums),
    sas_vars(Vs?, E?, Nums?, Vars),
    sas_cons(Cn?, E?, Vs?, Cn1),
    sas_schema2(L?, T?, Nm?, Vars?, Cn1?, Rs?, S).

procedure sas_schema2(Ans?, Ans?, Constant?, Args?, Constraint?, NRoleSpecs?, NSchema).
sas_schema2(no, yes, Nm, Vs, _, Rs, schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?)).
sas_schema2(yes, yes, Nm, Vs, _, Rs, cschema(Nm?, Vs?, [], Rs?)).
sas_schema2(_, no, Nm, Vs, Cn, Rs, nschema(Nm?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)).

% --- What the clause syntax requires, and its reading cannot carry ---------
% Each fault names the schema.  not_holder(Schema, Pred): an atom whose
% first argument is not a name of the schema ("the first argument of each
% its holder", Section 3.2; def:role).  not_in_vars(Schema, Pred): an
% argument of an atom of Pred, its multiplicity or its condition, or of the
% constraint (Pred constraint), that is a constant neither the wildcard, a
% role, nor a variable of Vars (def:schema: "its variables are its agent
% variables that are not agent roles and its speech-act variables";
% def:numbers, its value variables); a value variable, a speech-act variable
% of a name term or of a signed term, and a variable of Vars no atom writes
% are decided by the checker as before (not_in_head, head_not_variable).
% deleted_not_required(Schema, Role, Atom): an atom of -(i) not in =(i)
% (def:schema: "It is required that -(i) is a subset of =(i)").
% quantified_condition(Schema, X): the conjuncts over X not over one
% condition rho(pi, x, u_2, ..., u_r) (def:role: "over one variable x and
% one condition").  quantified_holder(Schema, X, Pred): a literal of a
% conjunct over X whose holder is not X ("x the holder of every literal
% L_j", def:role).  listed_agent_role(Schema, X): X quantified and the
% holder of a literal outside its conjuncts, so an agent role too.
% not_in_names(Schema, X): X quantified and not among the names.
% guard_not_role(Schema, Name): a guard that is no role ("G a set of agent
% roles of it", def:schema); a listed role among the guards is refused by
% the checker (listed_guarded).

procedure sas_fapp(Faults?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_fapp([], T, T?).
sas_fapp([F|Fs], T, [F?|R?]) :- sas_fapp(Fs?, T?, R).

% The plain literals whose holder is no name.
procedure sas_holder_faults(SQLits?, Constant?, Names?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_holder_faults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_holder_faults([L|Ls], Nm, Ns, T, R?) :- ground(L?), ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?) |
    sas_lit_atom(L?, A),
    sas_atom_named(A?, Ns?, Ok),
    sas_holder_faults(Ls?, Nm?, Ns?, T?, R1),
    sas_holder_fault(Ok?, Nm?, L?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_atom_named(SAtom?, Names?, Ans).
sas_atom_named(atom(_, []), _, no).
sas_atom_named(atom(_, [H|_]), Ns, R?) :- sas_in_names(H?, Ns?, R).

procedure sas_holder_fault(Ans?, Constant?, SQLit?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_holder_fault(yes, _, _, T, T?).
sas_holder_fault(no, Nm, L, T, [not_holder(Nm?, P?)|T?]) :-
    sas_lit_atom(L?, A),
    sas_pred(A?, P).

% The literals of a conjunct over X whose holder is not X.
procedure sas_qholder_faults(Quants?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qholder_faults([], _, T, T?).
sas_qholder_faults([q(X, _, Q)|Qs], Nm, T, R?) :- ground(Nm?) |
    sas_qholder_faults(Qs?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_qholder_faults1(Q?, Nm?, X?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_qholder_faults1(SQLits?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qholder_faults1([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_qholder_faults1([L|Ls], Nm, X, T, R?) :- ground(L?), ground(Nm?), ground(X?) |
    sas_lit_held(L?, X?, A),
    sas_lit_atom(L?, At),
    sas_pred(At?, P),
    sas_qholder_faults1(Ls?, Nm?, X?, T?, R1),
    sas_qholder_fault(A?, Nm?, X?, P?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_qholder_fault(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qholder_fault(yes, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qholder_fault(no, Nm, X, P, T, [quantified_holder(Nm?, X?, P?)|T?]).

% The constants of Vars an argument needs (not_in_vars).
procedure sas_arg_vf(SArg?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_arg_vf(own(_), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(ext(_, _), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(num(_), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(sgn(_, _), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(C, E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare_vf(C?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).

procedure(X) sas_bare_vf(X?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_bare_vf(C, _, _, _, _, T, T?) :- C? =?= '_' | true.
sas_bare_vf(C, E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- otherwise, ground(C?) |
    sas_look(C?, E?, L),
    sas_var(C?, V?, F),
    sas_bare_vf1(L?, F?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).

procedure sas_bare_vf1(Look?, VFound?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_bare_vf1(lrole(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_bare_vf1(lvar, vfound(_), _, _, T, T?).
sas_bare_vf1(lnone, vfound(_), _, _, T, T?).
sas_bare_vf1(lvar, vnone, Nm, P, T, [not_in_vars(Nm?, P?)|T?]).
sas_bare_vf1(lnone, vnone, Nm, P, T, [not_in_vars(Nm?, P?)|T?]).

procedure sas_args_vf(SArgs?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_args_vf([], _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_args_vf([A|As], E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?), ground(P?) |
    sas_args_vf(As?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R1),
    sas_arg_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, R1?, R).

% An atom's arguments after its holder, and a multiplicity.
procedure sas_atom_vf(SAtom?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_atom_vf(atom(_, []), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_atom_vf(atom(P, [_|As]), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_args_vf(As?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).

procedure sas_mult_vf(SMult?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_mult_vf(atom(P, As), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_atom_vf(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R).
sas_mult_vf(times(K, atom(P, As)), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?), ground(P?) |
    sas_atom_vf(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_arg_vf(K?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_lits_vf(SQLits?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_lits_vf([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_lits_vf([L|Ls], E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(L?), ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_lit_mult(L?, M),
    sas_lits_vf(Ls?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_mult_vf(M?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).

% A condition's arguments after its holder and its variable.
procedure sas_quants_vf(Quants?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_quants_vf([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_quants_vf([q(_, C, Q)|Qs], E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_quants_vf(Qs?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_lits_vf(Q?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R2),
    sas_cond_vf(C?, E?, V?, Nm?, R2?, R).

procedure sas_cond_vf(SAtom?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_cond_vf(atom(P, [_, _|Us]), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_args_vf(Us?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).
sas_cond_vf(_, _, _, _, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_cons_vf(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_cons_vf(true, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_cons_vf(and(A, B), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_cons_vf(B?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_cons_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(or(A, B), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_cons_vf(B?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_cons_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(eq(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(le(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(lt(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(ge(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(gt(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(succ(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_arg_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R1), sas_arg_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(signed(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_arg_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R1), sas_arg_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(unsigned(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_arg_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R1), sas_arg_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, R1?, R).

procedure sas_expr_vf(SExpr?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_expr_vf(plus(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_expr_vf(minus(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_expr_vf(mul(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_expr_vf(own(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(ext(_, _), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(num(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(sgn(_, _), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(C, E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare_vf(C?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R).

% The atoms each role deletes that it does not require.
procedure sas_del_faults(REnts?, Constant?, SCtx?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_del_faults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_del_faults([ar(N, I)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- ground(Nm?), ground(C?) |
    sas_rs(N?, C?, _, M),
    sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R1),
    sas_mfaults(M?, Nm?, I?, R1?, R).
sas_del_faults([lr(N, I)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- ground(Nm?), ground(C?) |
    sas_crs(N?, C?, _, M),
    sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R1),
    sas_mfaults(M?, Nm?, I?, R1?, R).
sas_del_faults([av(_)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R).

procedure sas_mfaults(Mults?, Constant?, Integer?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_mfaults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_mfaults([atom(P, As)|Ms], Nm, I, T, [deleted_not_required(Nm?, I?, atom(P?, As?))|R?]) :-
    ground(Nm?), integer(I?) | sas_mfaults(Ms?, Nm?, I?, T?, R).
sas_mfaults([times(_, A)|Ms], Nm, I, T, [deleted_not_required(Nm?, I?, A?)|R?]) :-
    ground(Nm?), integer(I?) | sas_mfaults(Ms?, Nm?, I?, T?, R).

% The quantified variables, each once: one condition rho(pi, X, ...), X no
% agent role, X among the names.
procedure sas_qvars(Quants?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_qvars([], T, T?).
sas_qvars([q(X, _, _)|Qs], T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(T?) |
    sas_in(X?, T?, A),
    sas_qvars1(A?, X?, Qs?, T?, R).

procedure sas_qvars1(Ans?, Constant?, Quants?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_qvars1(yes, _, Qs, T, R?) :- sas_qvars(Qs?, T?, R).
sas_qvars1(no, X, Qs, T, R?) :- sas_qvars(Qs?, [X?|T?], R).

procedure sas_cond_ok(SAtoms?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_cond_ok([atom(Rho, [P, Y|Us])|Cs], X, R?) :- Y? =?= X?, ground(Rho?), ground(P?), ground(Y?), ground(Us?) |
    sas_conds_same(Cs?, atom(Rho?, [P?, Y?|Us?]), R).
sas_cond_ok(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_conds_same(SAtoms?, SAtom?, Ans).
sas_conds_same([], _, yes).
sas_conds_same([C|Cs], C0, R?) :- C? =?= C0? | sas_conds_same(Cs?, C0?, R).
sas_conds_same(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_qfaults(PNames?, Constant?, Quants?, SQLits?, Names?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qfaults([], _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qfaults([X|Xs], Nm, QQ, PP, Ns, T, R?) :-
    ground(X?), ground(Nm?), ground(QQ?), ground(PP?), ground(Ns?) |
    sas_conds(QQ?, X?, Cs),
    sas_cond_ok(Cs?, X?, C),
    sas_holds(PP?, X?, A),
    sas_in_names(X?, Ns?, In),
    sas_qfaults(Xs?, Nm?, QQ?, PP?, Ns?, T?, F0),
    sas_qf1(C?, Nm?, X?, F0?, F1),
    sas_qf2(A?, Nm?, X?, F1?, F2),
    sas_qf3(In?, Nm?, X?, F2?, R).

procedure sas_qf1(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qf1(yes, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qf1(no, Nm, X, T, [quantified_condition(Nm?, X?)|T?]).

procedure sas_qf2(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qf2(no, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qf2(yes, Nm, X, T, [listed_agent_role(Nm?, X?)|T?]).

procedure sas_qf3(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qf3(yes, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qf3(no, Nm, X, T, [not_in_names(Nm?, X?)|T?]).

% The guards, each a role.
procedure sas_gfaults(PNames?, Constant?, REnts?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_gfaults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_gfaults([G|Gs], Nm, E, T, R?) :- ground(G?), ground(Nm?), ground(E?) |
    sas_look(G?, E?, L),
    sas_gfaults(Gs?, Nm?, E?, T?, R1),
    sas_gfault(L?, Nm?, G?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_gfault(Look?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_gfault(lrole(_), _, _, T, T?).
sas_gfault(lvar, Nm, G, T, [guard_not_role(Nm?, G?)|T?]).
sas_gfault(lnone, Nm, G, T, [guard_not_role(Nm?, G?)|T?]).

% The faults of the reading of a schema written as a clause, in the order:
% the holders, the variables, the deleted atoms, the quantified conjuncts,
% the guards.
procedure sas_faults(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, PNames?, Faults).
sas_faults(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G, R?) :-
    sas_split(H?, HP, HQ),
    sas_split(B?, BP, BQ),
    sas_faults0(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, Cn?, G?, R).

procedure sas_faults0(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SQLits?, Quants?, SQLits?, Quants?, SConstraint?, PNames?, Faults).
sas_faults0(Nm, Ns, Vs, HP, HQ, BP, BQ, Cn, G, R?) :-
    ground(Ns?), ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?) |
    sas_qapp(HP?, BP?, PP1),
    sas_qapp(HP?, BP?, PP2),
    sas_quapp(HQ?, BQ?, QQ1),
    sas_quapp(HQ?, BQ?, QQ2),
    sas_table(Ns?, PP1?, QQ1?, 1, E),
    sas_faults1(Nm?, Ns?, PP2?, QQ2?, Cn?, sctx(HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, G?, E?, Vs?), R).

procedure sas_faults1(Constant?, Names?, SQLits?, Quants?, SConstraint?, SCtx?, Faults).
sas_faults1(Nm, Ns, PP, QQ, Cn, sctx(HP, HQ, BP, BQ, G, E, Vs), R?) :-
    ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?), ground(PP?), ground(QQ?), ground(HP?), ground(HQ?),
    ground(BP?), ground(BQ?), ground(G?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_qvars(QQ?, [], Xs),
    sas_gfaults(G?, Nm?, E?, [], F5),
    sas_qfaults(Xs?, Nm?, QQ?, PP?, Ns?, F5?, F4),
    sas_del_faults(E?, Nm?, sctx(HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, G?, E?, Vs?), F4?, F3),
    sas_cons_vf(Cn?, E?, Vs?, Nm?, F3?, F2c),
    sas_quants_vf(QQ?, E?, Vs?, Nm?, F2c?, F2b),
    sas_lits_vf(PP?, E?, Vs?, Nm?, F2b?, F2),
    sas_qholder_faults(QQ?, Nm?, F2?, F1),
    sas_holder_faults(PP?, Nm?, Ns?, F1?, R).

% The faults of the reading of a contract: those of each schema written as a
% clause, none of a schema written in the checker's form.
procedure wsch_faults(WSchema?, Faults).
wsch_faults(sas(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G), R?) :- sas_faults(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, H?, B?, Cn?, G?, R).
wsch_faults(_, []) :- otherwise | true.

procedure wcontract_faults(WContract?, Faults).
wcontract_faults([], []).
wcontract_faults([S|Ss], R?) :-
    wsch_faults(S?, F1),
    wcontract_faults(Ss?, F2),
    sas_fapp(F1?, F2?, R).

procedure wbody_faults(WBody?, Faults).
wbody_faults([], []).
wbody_faults([S|Ss], R?) :- wcontract_faults([S?|Ss?], R).
wbody_faults(reflexive(_, Ss), R?) :- wcontract_faults(Ss?, R).

procedure read_faults(WDeclared?, Faults).
read_faults([], []).
read_faults([S|Ss], R?) :- wcontract_faults([S?|Ss?], R).
read_faults(reflexive(_, Ss), R?) :- wcontract_faults(Ss?, R).
read_faults(environment(_, B), R?) :- wbody_faults(B?, R).

% --- The image of a binding (def:schema, def:binding) ----------------------
% People and speech acts are numbered; person(0) and person(1) are the two
% the conditions quantify over.  signed(S, P) is the image of a signed term,
% the pair of the speech act S and the person P in its role
% (def:binding).  undef marks a variable that a partial substitution leaves
% unbound and occurs in no completed one.  nval(N) is the image of a value
% argument that is the number N, or a value variable a binding sends to N;
% nfree(X) is the image of the value variable X of the introductory act,
% whose value its introduction chooses (def:binding-numbers): a match that
% meets it records the equation it rests on (Eqs, below), which the values
% chosen must satisfy (unobstructed.glp).  A value names no agent (GSC,
% Section 3.2), so neither names anyone.
Val   ::= person(Integer) ; speech(Integer) ; signed(Val, Val) ; undef
        ; nval(Constant) ; nfree(Constant).
Vals  ::= [] ; [Val | Vals].
GAtom ::= gatom(Constant, Vals).

Bind     ::= bind(Arg, Val).
Subst    ::= [] ; [Bind | Subst].
Substs   ::= [] ; [Subst | Substs].
Found    ::= bound(Val) ; free.
% match(S, E): the atoms match under S where the equations E between values
% hold, each between two images of value arguments, nval or nfree.
Eq       ::= eqv(Val, Val).
Eqs      ::= [] ; [Eq | Eqs].
MatchRes ::= match(Subst, Eqs) ; nomatch.

% --- What clause 2 of def:unobstructed is decided against ------------------
% The other party of the introduction, and the first unused name index.
Ctx ::= ctx(Val, Integer).

% --- Verdicts --------------------------------------------------------------
Ans   ::= yes ; no.
Ints  ::= [] ; [Integer | Ints].
Preds ::= [] ; [Constant | Preds].
% listed_role(Schema, Role, Atom) is the first part of clause 2 of
% def:unobstructed: the listed role Role of Schema adds Atom, of the
% predicate of an atom the introductory act forbids at a role.
Cause ::= unobtainable ; blocked_by(Constant, Integer, Atom) ; reflexive ; environment
        ; listed_role(Constant, Integer, Atom).
% What GAI's Definition Speech-act schema requires of a signed term, and the atom
% carrying one violates: it occurs in an atom not marked + (not_added), its
% speech-act variable occurs in no atom its role requires (not_required), or
% its role is not an agent role (not_agent_role).
SgnCause ::= not_added ; not_required ; not_agent_role.
% What def:schema requires of the form of a schema, and a schema formed
% otherwise violates: an atom both added and deleted at a role
% (added_and_deleted), and no role adding or deleting an atom
% (no_role_changes).  What def:volition requires of a reading role (GSC
% 0380a8a), a role that is not guarding and adds and deletes nothing: an
% edge to a guarding role from an atom that guarding role requires; a
% reading role with none is a fault changes_nothing(Schema, Role) of
% volition, in a verdict not_grassroots.  What def:volition requires of a
% schema with no guarding role and a reading role (GSC c100cdc): a signature
% atom (def:signature), so one with none is a fault
% no_signature_atom(Schema), and only agent roles as reading roles, so each
% listed reading role is a fault listed_reading(Schema, Role), in a verdict
% not_grassroots.  What def:schema requires of a schema's head, its
% variables x_1, ..., x_m distinct agent and speech-act variables and its
% atoms over its roles, those variables and its signed terms: an entry of
% the head that is not a variable (head_not_variable), an entry listed twice
% (head_repeated), and a variable of the schema not in its head
% (not_in_head).  What def:role requires of a name term, <pi> for an agent
% role pi of its schema or sigma.y for a name term sigma of it: a name term
% whose base is not an agent role of its schema (name_term_base), naming the
% schema and the name term.  What def:role requires of a listed role
% pi[rho(*, u_2, ..., u_r)], and one violates: pi an agent role of its
% schema (listed_base), and u_2, ..., u_r arguments of the schema, a signed
% term (GAI's) occurring only in an atom marked +, so no signed term among
% them (listed_signed); each names the schema and the listed role.  What
% def:schema requires of the mark ?, that only an agent role carry it: a
% listed role carrying it (listed_guarded).  What GSC's passage on numbers
% (Section 3.2, def:numbers, GSC 859a007) requires of them: a multiplicity
% on an atom added, deleted or required, so one on an atom forbidden is a
% fault multiplicity_forbidden(Schema, Role, Atom); a multiplicity a positive whole number or a value variable, so one that is
% no value argument is a fault multiplicity_not_numeric(Schema, Role, Atom),
% and one that is a number and no positive whole number a fault
% multiplicity_not_whole(Schema, Role, Atom); a multiplicity only on an atom
% with no wildcard (def:numbers, GSC 593e8a7), so one on an
% atom carrying the wildcard, a cleared atom, is a fault
% multiplicity_wildcard(Schema, Role, Atom); and a
% constraint on the schema's value variables, so an argument of the
% constraint that is no value argument is a fault
% constraint_not_numeric(Schema, Arg).  A value variable is a variable of
% the schema, listed in its head like the others (not_in_head,
% head_repeated), and a number in the head is no variable
% (head_not_variable).  What def:schema requires of a cleared atom (GSC
% 327e035): the wildcard only in an atom marked -, so an atom marked +, not
% or unmarked carrying it is a fault wildcard(Schema, Role, Atom), and a
% listed role carrying it among its arguments, which are arguments of the
% schema (def:role), a fault listed_wildcard(Schema, Role); and no atom of
% +(i) obtained from an atom of *(i) by replacing its wildcards, so each such
% atom added is a fault added_and_cleared(Schema, Role, Atom).  What
% def:numbers requires of a signing condition signed(u, y) or unsigned(u, y)
% (GSC 10fcc92): u an agent role or agent variable, so any other u is a fault
% signing_not_agent(Schema, U); and y a speech-act variable, so any other y is
% a fault signing_not_speech_act(Schema, Y); a variable among them that the
% head does not list is a fault not_in_head(Schema, Var).
Fault ::= no_introductory_act
        ; obstructed(Constant, Integer, Atom, Cause)
        ; untraceable(Preds)
        ; volition(Constant, Integer, Integer)
        ; reflexive(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; signed(Constant, Integer, Atom, SgnCause)
        ; added_and_deleted(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; added_and_cleared(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; wildcard(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; listed_wildcard(Constant, Integer)
        ; changes_nothing(Constant, Integer)
        ; listed_reading(Constant, Integer)
        ; no_signature_atom(Constant)
        ; no_role_changes(Constant)
        ; head_not_variable(Constant, Arg)
        ; head_repeated(Constant, Arg)
        ; not_in_head(Constant, Arg)
        ; name_term_base(Constant, NameTerm)
        ; listed_base(Constant, Integer)
        ; listed_signed(Constant, Integer)
        ; listed_guarded(Constant, Integer)
        ; multiplicity_forbidden(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; multiplicity_not_numeric(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; multiplicity_not_whole(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; multiplicity_wildcard(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; constraint_not_numeric(Constant, Arg)
        ; constraint_not_linear(Constant, Expr)
        ; constraint_not_conjunction(Constant, Constraint)
        ; signing_not_agent(Constant, Arg)
        ; signing_not_speech_act(Constant, Arg)
        ; obstructed_jointly(Constant)
        ; not_holder(Constant, Constant)
        ; not_in_vars(Constant, Constant)
        ; deleted_not_required(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; quantified_condition(Constant, Constant)
        ; quantified_holder(Constant, Constant, Constant)
        ; listed_agent_role(Constant, Constant)
        ; not_in_names(Constant, Constant)
        ; guard_not_role(Constant, Constant).
Faults  ::= [] ; [Fault | Faults].
% What def:signature is decided against (volition.glp): sig(Is, Vs), the
% indices of a schema's agent roles and its variables.
SigCtx  ::= sig(Ints, Args).

% --- What an introduction with wards is made of (GAI, "Contracts with Wards")
% guardianship(M, Iota, G, W, V) is the guardianship (m, iota, g, w, v) of
% def:guardianship; a party of a relay act (def:relay) is a ward role,
% ward(Role, Mark, GuardianRole), or a free role, free(Role); a relay act is
% named with its two parties.  An introduction with wards
% (def:introduction-wards) names the introductory act unobstructed but for
% the marks, the set of marks, the guardianship of each and the relay acts
% found: for each mark one with a free role, and for each pair of marks, in
% the order of the set, one with a ward role of each; and the leaving marks
% of the contract (def:leaving), in the order of its marks.
Guardianship  ::= guardianship(Constant, Constant, Constant, Constant, Constant).
Guardianships ::= [] ; [Guardianship | Guardianships].
Party  ::= ward(Integer, Constant, Integer) ; free(Integer).
Parties ::= [] ; [Party | Parties].
Relay  ::= relay(Constant, Party, Party).
Relays ::= [] ; [Relay | Relays].
Wards  ::= introduction_with_wards(Constant, Preds, Guardianships, Relays, Preds)
         ; no_introduction_with_wards.
% h(Schema, Role, H): the relay act Schema requires at its ward role Role an atom of the predicate H that clause 2 of def:relay admits as an atom of h and as nothing else (GSC 410a440).
RelayH  ::= h(Constant, Integer, Constant).
RelayHs ::= [] ; [RelayH | RelayHs].
% The leaving marks of a contract for a set M of marks (def:leaving) depend
% on the guardianship of each mark in M: leaving(Gs, Ls) holds the
% guardianships taken, one per mark, and the leaving marks for them.
Leaving  ::= leaving(Guardianships, Preds).
Leavings ::= [] ; [Leaving | Leavings].

% What the search of wards.glp carries: the sets of marks it tries, the
% guardianship candidates of each mark of a set, the kind of each role of a
% schema put to def:relay -- a ward role of a mark with its guardian role, a
% free role, a guardian role, or none of these -- the kind of party sought,
% and an introductory act unobstructed but for the marks with its predicate e.
PredSets   ::= [] ; [Preds | PredSets].
GuardLists ::= [] ; [Guardianships | GuardLists].
RK   ::= rk_ward(Constant, Integer) ; rk_free ; rk_guard ; rk_other.
RKs  ::= [] ; [RK | RKs].
Kind ::= free_party ; ward_party(Constant).
IntroE ::= intro(Constant, Constant) ; no_intro.

% syntactically_grassroots is the verdict on a contract that is so by
% def:syntactically-grassroots, of agent roles and listed roles alike (GSC
% ac7ad63).  grassroots_with_wards is the verdict on a contract with no
% listed role and no name term that is grassroots with wards by GAI's
% appendix "Contracts with Wards", and syntactically_grassroots_with_wards
% the verdict on one with them that is syntactically grassroots with wards by
% def:sg-wards of CSSN's paper, naming what grassroots_with_wards names.
Verdict ::= syntactically_grassroots ; not_grassroots(Faults)
          ; syntactically_grassroots_with_wards(Constant, Preds, Guardianships, Relays, Preds)
          ; grassroots_with_wards(Constant, Preds, Guardianships, Relays, Preds)
          ; malformed(Faults).

% The introductory acts of a contract, for inspection (def:introduction,
% def:unobstructed): intro_act(Schema, Status), each schema that is an
% introductory act, Status unobstructed where some introduction of it meets
% def:unobstructed, and obstructed(Faults) otherwise, the faults of its first
% introduction.
IntroStatus ::= unobstructed ; obstructed(Faults).
IntroAct    ::= intro_act(Constant, IntroStatus).
IntroActs   ::= [] ; [IntroAct | IntroActs].

% What an introduction is decided by (unobstructed.glp): an introduction
% meeting def:unobstructed (t_ok), the faults where none does (t_bad), or
% none at all (t_none); the act, its plain form, the contract as written and
% plain, and its reflexive predicates (IntroCtx); and each condition the
% clauses put to its values, with the fault it is where no choice of them
% meets it (Item): an atom required at a role, with the formula saying that
% a schema of arity one supplies it; an atom forbidden at a role, with the
% bindings of other schemas adding it (Blk, each the formula saying where
% it adds it) and the formula saying that none does; or a fault the values
% do not touch.
Try      ::= t_ok ; t_bad(Faults) ; t_none.
IntroCtx ::= ic(Schema, NSchema, NContract, Contract, Preds).
Blk      ::= blk(Constant, Integer, Atom, DNF).
Blks     ::= [] ; [Blk | Blks].
Item     ::= it_req(Integer, Atom, DNF) ; it_forb(Integer, Atom, Blks, DNF)
           ; it_fault(Fault).
Items    ::= [] ; [Item | Items].
% How the value variables of another schema's binding are named: those of a
% schema of arity one supplying the atom Is names, or those of a schema
% whose bindings are eliminated (Name, below).  Two images are equal where
% the atoms of a conjunction hold, or never (eqr_no).
Tg       ::= tg_sv(Ints) ; tg_bv.
EqR      ::= eqr(Conj) ; eqr_no.
Cand    ::= none ; some(Faults).
Missing ::= missing(Integer) ; all_reached.

% --- Linear arithmetic over the values (linear.glp) ------------------------
% A variable over the values: q(N) ranges over the rationals and z(N) over
% the whole numbers, a multiplicity carrying its bound N >= 1 as an atom.
% Its name: iv(X), the value variable X of the introductory act; sv(Is, X),
% the value variable X of a schema of arity one supplying the atom Is names;
% bv(X), the value variable X of a schema whose bindings are eliminated
% (linear.glp, elim_block); and nv(X) and fv(X), the whole and the
% fractional parts of the act's rational value X.  A linear form is
% lin(Terms, C), the sum of each term's coefficient times its variable,
% plus C, all whole numbers; an atom is geq(L), L >= 0, grt(L), L > 0,
% equ(L), L = 0, or dvd(M, L), M divides L; a conjunction is a list of atoms
% and a formula a list of conjunctions, their disjunction.
Name      ::= iv(Constant) ; sv(Ints, Constant) ; bv(Constant) ; nv(Constant)
            ; fv(Constant).
Var       ::= q(Name) ; z(Name).
Vars      ::= [] ; [Var | Vars].
Term      ::= t(Var, Integer).
Terms     ::= [] ; [Term | Terms].
Lin       ::= lin(Terms, Integer).
LAtom     ::= geq(Lin) ; grt(Lin) ; equ(Lin) ; dvd(Integer, Lin).
Conj      ::= [] ; [LAtom | Conj].
DNF       ::= [] ; [Conj | DNF].
DNFs      ::= [] ; [DNF | DNFs].
Constants ::= [] ; [Constant | Constants].
% What linear.glp carries: a conjunction simplified, or false; the truth of
% an atom, settled or open; an expression, the form divided by a positive
% whole number, or none where it is not linear; the variables a constraint's
% value variables are read as; an equation found, with the rest of its
% conjunction; the kind of variable sought; a bound on V' = d.V of Cooper's
% method, Sign.V' + t of its kind; a value of the ceiling, the floor or the
% value of a sum of fractional parts, with the atoms that say so; and the
% direction a bound is met from.
CS        ::= cs(Conj) ; cs_false.
LTv       ::= lt_true ; lt_false ; lt_open.
Ex        ::= ex(Lin, Integer) ; ex_bad.
VBind     ::= vb(Constant, Var).
VEnv      ::= [] ; [VBind | VEnv].
FoundEq   ::= fe(Lin, Conj) ; fe_none(Conj).
VSel      ::= sel_q ; sel_z ; sel_bq ; sel_bz.
VPick     ::= pick(Var) ; pick_none.
BKind     ::= b_geq ; b_grt ; b_dvd(Integer).
Bd        ::= bd(BKind, Integer, Lin).
Bds       ::= [] ; [Bd | Bds].
QKind     ::= ceil_case ; floor_case ; eq_case.
QCase     ::= qc(Integer, Conj).
QCases    ::= [] ; [QCase | QCases].
Dir       ::= low ; up.

% --- What def:grounded is decided against, for one schema ----------------
% The bases of its roles, the bases of the arguments of the atoms of Phi_E it
% requires, the speech-act variables occurring in those atoms, and the
% speech-act variables occurring in any atom it requires.
PCtx ::= pctx(Bases, Bases, Args, Args).

% --- The LaTeX of a compiled schema (def:compile) -------------------------
% GLP has no string concatenation, so a display is carried as its tokens and
% printed one to a line; a newline is whitespace to LaTeX, so the lines are
% the display.  ChunkLists holds the conjuncts of the proviso, each a display
% of its own, before they are joined.
Chunks     ::= [] ; [Constant | Chunks].
ChunkLists ::= [] ; [Chunks | ChunkLists].
FoundS     ::= found(Schema) ; not_found.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Booleans
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure both_yes(Ans?, Ans?, Ans).
both_yes(yes, A, A?).
both_yes(no, _, no).

procedure or_yes(Ans?, Ans?, Ans).
or_yes(yes, _, yes).
or_yes(no, A, A?).

procedure flip(Ans?, Ans).
flip(yes, no).
flip(no, yes).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Lists
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure args_app(Args?, Args?, Args).
args_app([], T, T?).
args_app([A|As], T, [A?|R?]) :- args_app(As?, T?, R).

procedure atoms_app(Atoms?, Atoms?, Atoms).
atoms_app([], T, T?).
atoms_app([A|As], T, [A?|R?]) :- atoms_app(As?, T?, R).

procedure preds_app(Preds?, Preds?, Preds).
preds_app([], T, T?).
preds_app([P|Ps], T, [P?|R?]) :- preds_app(Ps?, T?, R).

procedure nterms_app(NameTerms?, NameTerms?, NameTerms).
nterms_app([], T, T?).
nterms_app([N|Ns], T, [N?|R?]) :- nterms_app(Ns?, T?, R).

procedure bases_app(Bases?, Bases?, Bases).
bases_app([], T, T?).
bases_app([B|Bs], T, [B?|R?]) :- bases_app(Bs?, T?, R).

procedure faults_app(Faults?, Faults?, Faults).
faults_app([], T, T?).
faults_app([F|Fs], T, [F?|R?]) :- faults_app(Fs?, T?, R).

procedure contract_app(Contract?, Contract?, Contract).
contract_app([], T, T?).
contract_app([S|Ss], T, [S?|R?]) :- contract_app(Ss?, T?, R).

procedure preds_len(Preds?, Integer).
preds_len([], 0).
preds_len([_|Xs], N?) :- preds_len(Xs?, M), N := M? + 1.

procedure roles_len(RoleSpecs?, Integer).
roles_len([], 0).
roles_len([_|Xs], N?) :- roles_len(Xs?, M), N := M? + 1.

procedure ints_len(Ints?, Integer).
ints_len([], 0).
ints_len([_|Xs], N?) :- ints_len(Xs?, M), N := M? + 1.

procedure pred_member(Constant?, Preds?, Ans).
pred_member(_, [], no).
pred_member(P, [Q|_], yes) :- P? =?= Q? | true.
pred_member(P, [_|Qs], R?) :- otherwise | pred_member(P?, Qs?, R).

procedure args_member(Args?, Arg?, Ans).
args_member([], _, no).
args_member([A|_], U, yes) :- A? =?= U? | true.
args_member([_|As], U, R?) :- otherwise | args_member(As?, U?, R).

procedure base_member(Bases?, Base?, Ans).
base_member([], _, no).
base_member([B|_], C, yes) :- B? =?= C? | true.
base_member([_|Bs], C, R?) :- otherwise | base_member(Bs?, C?, R).

procedure nt_member(NameTerms?, NameTerm?, Ans).
nt_member([], _, no).
nt_member([N|_], M, yes) :- N? =?= M? | true.
nt_member([_|Ns], M, R?) :- otherwise | nt_member(Ns?, M?, R).

procedure vals_member(Vals?, Val?, Ans).
vals_member([], _, no).
vals_member([V|_], W, yes) :- V? =?= W? | true.
vals_member([_|Vs], W, R?) :- otherwise | vals_member(Vs?, W?, R).

procedure ints_member(Ints?, Integer?, Ans).
ints_member([], _, no).
ints_member([I|_], J, yes) :- I? =:= J? | true.
ints_member([_|Is], J, R?) :- otherwise | ints_member(Is?, J?, R).

% args_remove(As, A, R): every occurrence of A dropped from As.
procedure args_remove(Args?, Arg?, Args).
args_remove([], _, []).
args_remove([B|As], A, R?) :- B? =?= A? | args_remove(As?, A?, R).
args_remove([B|As], A, [B?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(B?) | args_remove(As?, A?, R).

procedure args_dedup(Args?, Args).
args_dedup([], []).
args_dedup([A|As], [A?|R?]) :- ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    args_remove(As?, A?, As1),
    args_dedup(As1?, R).

procedure preds_remove(Preds?, Constant?, Preds).
preds_remove([], _, []).
preds_remove([Q|Ps], P, R?) :- Q? =?= P? | preds_remove(Ps?, P?, R).
preds_remove([Q|Ps], P, [Q?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(Q?) | preds_remove(Ps?, P?, R).

procedure preds_dedup(Preds?, Preds).
preds_dedup([], []).
preds_dedup([P|Ps], [P?|R?]) :- ground(P?), ground(Ps?) |
    preds_remove(Ps?, P?, Ps1),
    preds_dedup(Ps1?, R).

% preds_diff(Ps, E, R): the members of Ps not in E, in the order of Ps.
procedure preds_diff1(Ans?, Constant?, Preds?, Preds?, Preds).
preds_diff1(yes, _, Ps, E, R?) :- ground(Ps?), ground(E?) | preds_diff(Ps?, E?, R).
preds_diff1(no, P, Ps, E, [P?|R?]) :- ground(Ps?), ground(E?) | preds_diff(Ps?, E?, R).

procedure preds_diff(Preds?, Preds?, Preds).
preds_diff([], _, []).
preds_diff([P|Ps], E, R?) :- ground(P?), ground(Ps?), ground(E?) |
    pred_member(P?, E?, A),
    preds_diff1(A?, P?, Ps?, E?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Substitutions
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure subst_lookup(Subst?, Arg?, Found).
subst_lookup([], _, free).
subst_lookup([bind(A, V)|_], B, bound(V?)) :- A? =?= B? | true.
subst_lookup([bind(_, _)|S], B, R?) :- otherwise | subst_lookup(S?, B?, R).

procedure subst_app(Subst?, Subst?, Subst).
subst_app([], T, T?).
subst_app([B|Bs], T, [B?|R?]) :- subst_app(Bs?, T?, R).

procedure unwrap_val(Found?, Val).
unwrap_val(bound(V), V?).
unwrap_val(free, undef).

% apply_arg/apply_atom: the image under a binding, written beta(phi) in
% Section 3.  A completed substitution binds every variable of the schema, so
% undef never reaches an atom.  The image of a signed term is the pair of the
% speech act its variable maps to and the person in its role (def:binding).
procedure apply_arg(Subst?, Arg?, Val).
apply_arg(S, sgn(Y, J), signed(SV?, PV?)) :- ground(S?), ground(Y?), integer(J?) |
    apply_arg(S?, svar(Y?), SV),
    apply_arg(S?, role(J?), PV).
apply_arg(S, num(X), V?) :- ground(S?), ground(X?) | apply_num(S?, X?, V).
apply_arg(S, A, V?) :- otherwise, ground(S?), ground(A?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, A?, F),
    unwrap_val(F?, V).

% The image of a value argument (GSC, Section 3.2): the number itself, or
% what the binding sends the value variable to; one the binding leaves free
% is written nfree, as a value not yet chosen.
procedure apply_num(Subst?, Constant?, Val).
apply_num(_, X, nval(X?)) :- number(X?) | true.
apply_num(S, X, V?) :- otherwise, ground(S?), ground(X?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, num(X?), F),
    unwrap_num(F?, X?, V).

procedure unwrap_num(Found?, Constant?, Val).
unwrap_num(bound(V), _, V?).
unwrap_num(free, X, nfree(X?)).

procedure apply_args(Subst?, Args?, Vals).
apply_args(_, [], []).
apply_args(S, [A|As], [V?|Vs?]) :- ground(S?), ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    apply_arg(S?, A?, V),
    apply_args(S?, As?, Vs).

procedure apply_atom(Subst?, Atom?, GAtom).
apply_atom(S, atom(P, As), gatom(P?, Vs?)) :- ground(S?), ground(P?), ground(As?) |
    apply_args(S?, As?, Vs).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Matching a schema's atom against a ground one
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% match_atom(Psi, G, Rs, S, R): the bindings extending S under which Psi
% becomes G, if any, Rs being the roles of Psi's schema.  A binding sends
% roles and party variables to people, two roles to one person only if
% neither of them adds or deletes an atom naming the other, and speech-act
% variables to speech acts (def:binding); kind_ok and binding_ok below are
% exactly those requirements.

procedure kind_ok(Arg?, Val?, Ans).
kind_ok(role(_), person(_), yes).
kind_ok(role(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(role(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(role(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(role(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(role(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), person(_), yes).
kind_ok(pvar(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), speech(_), yes).
kind_ok(svar(_), signed(_, _), yes).
kind_ok(svar(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(svar(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), nfree(_), no).
% A signed term is matched by its two parts (match_sgn below), never here.
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), person(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), signed(_, _), yes).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), undef, no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), nfree(_), no).
% A value argument matches a number and nothing else (match_num below).
kind_ok(num(_), nval(_), yes).
kind_ok(num(_), nfree(_), yes).
kind_ok(num(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(num(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(num(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(num(_), undef, no).
% The wildcard occurs only in a cleared atom, which is matched by
% matches_cleared and never against a binding's image here.
kind_ok(any, _, no).

% roles_at(S, V, Js): the indices of the roles S sends to V.  Clause 2 of
% def:unobstructed asks of the other party that one of them be no reading
% role (some_not_reading).
procedure roles_at(Subst?, Val?, Ints).
roles_at([], _, []).
roles_at([bind(role(J), W)|S], V, [J?|R?]) :- W? =?= V? | roles_at(S?, V?, R).
roles_at([bind(_, _)|S], V, R?) :- otherwise | roles_at(S?, V?, R).

% args_name_role(As, J, R): the arguments As name role J -- it is among them
% or is the role of a signed term among them (Section 3.1, what an atom
% names in a schema).
procedure arg_names_role(Arg?, Integer?, Ans).
arg_names_role(role(I), J, yes) :- I? =:= J? | true.
arg_names_role(sgn(_, I), J, yes) :- I? =:= J? | true.
arg_names_role(A, _, no) :- otherwise, ground(A?) | true.

procedure args_name_role1(Ans?, Args?, Integer?, Ans).
args_name_role1(yes, _, _, yes).
args_name_role1(no, As, J, R?) :- ground(As?), integer(J?) | args_name_role(As?, J?, R).

procedure args_name_role(Args?, Integer?, Ans).
args_name_role([], _, no).
args_name_role([A|As], J, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?), integer(J?) |
    arg_names_role(A?, J?, A1),
    args_name_role1(A1?, As?, J?, R).

% names_role(Phis, J, R): some atom of Phis names role J.
procedure names_role1(Ans?, Atoms?, Integer?, Ans).
names_role1(yes, _, _, yes).
names_role1(no, Xs, J, R?) :- ground(Xs?), integer(J?) | names_role(Xs?, J?, R).

procedure names_role(Atoms?, Integer?, Ans).
names_role([], _, no).
names_role([atom(_, As)|Xs], J, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(Xs?), integer(J?) |
    args_name_role(As?, J?, A),
    names_role1(A?, Xs?, J?, R).

% atoms_member(Phis, Phi, R): Phi is one of Phis.
procedure atoms_member(Atoms?, Atom?, Ans).
atoms_member([], _, no).
atoms_member([A|_], B, yes) :- A? =?= B? | true.
atoms_member([_|As], B, R?) :- otherwise | atoms_member(As?, B?, R).

% role_names(RS, J, R): the role adds or deletes an atom naming role J.  A
% cleared atom naming J, as unfriend's listed(Bob, *) at Alice, deletes every
% atom it matches (def:schema), each naming J, so it counts as deleting one.
procedure role_names(RoleSpec?, Integer?, Ans).
role_names(RS, J, R?) :- ground(RS?), integer(J?) |
    rs_add(RS?, P),
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    names_role(P?, J?, A1),
    names_role(M?, J?, A2),
    or_yes(A1?, A2?, R).

% may_share(Rs, J, K, R): a binding may send roles J and K to one person:
% neither of them adds or deletes an atom naming the other (def:binding).
procedure may_share(RoleSpecs?, Integer?, Integer?, Ans).
may_share(Rs, J, K, R?) :- ground(Rs?), integer(J?), integer(K?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, J?, RJ),
    nth_rs(Rs?, K?, RK),
    role_names(RJ?, K?, A1),
    role_names(RK?, J?, A2),
    or_yes(A1?, A2?, A),
    flip(A?, R).

procedure all_share1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Ints?, Integer?, Ans).
all_share1(no, _, _, _, no).
all_share1(yes, Rs, Js, K, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(Js?), integer(K?) |
    all_share(Rs?, Js?, K?, R).

% all_share(Rs, Js, K, R): role K may take the person of every role in Js.
procedure all_share(RoleSpecs?, Ints?, Integer?, Ans).
all_share(_, [], _, yes).
all_share(Rs, [J|Js], K, R?) :- ground(Rs?), integer(J?), ground(Js?), integer(K?) |
    may_share(Rs?, J?, K?, A),
    all_share1(A?, Rs?, Js?, K?, R).

% A role may take V when every role S already sends to V may share it.
procedure binding_ok(Arg?, Val?, Subst?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
binding_ok(role(K), V, S, Rs, R?) :- integer(K?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(Rs?) |
    roles_at(S?, V?, Js),
    all_share(Rs?, Js?, K?, R).
binding_ok(pvar(_), _, _, _, yes).
binding_ok(svar(_), _, _, _, yes).
binding_ok(nterm(_), _, _, _, yes).
% A signed term is no variable and is matched by its parts (match_sgn).
binding_ok(sgn(_, _), _, _, _, no).
% A value argument is matched by match_num, never here.
binding_ok(num(_), _, _, _, no).
binding_ok(any, _, _, _, no).

procedure match_bind(Ans?, Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_bind(yes, A, V, S, E, match([bind(A?, V?)|S?], E?)).
match_bind(no, _, _, _, _, nomatch).

procedure val_same(Val?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
val_same(W, V, S, E, match(S?, E?)) :- W? =?= V? | true.
val_same(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure match_one1(Found?, Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_one1(free, A, V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(A?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    kind_ok(A?, V?, K),
    binding_ok(A?, V?, S?, Rs?, I),
    both_yes(K?, I?, Ok),
    match_bind(Ok?, A?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_one1(bound(W), _, V, S, E, _, R?) :- ground(W?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    val_same(W?, V?, S?, E?, R).

% A signed term sgn(y, pi) matches a signed value by its two parts, the
% speech-act variable against the speech act and the role against the person
% (def:binding: beta(sgn(y, pi)) := (beta(y), beta(pi))), and matches no
% person and no speech act: the speech acts of an introduction are taken
% signed once (README, "One thing to know about the reading").
procedure match_sgn(Constant?, Integer?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_sgn(Y, J, signed(SV, PV), S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(Y?), integer(J?), ground(SV?), ground(PV?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_one(svar(Y?), SV?, S?, E?, Rs?, R1),
    match_rest(R1?, [role(J?)], [PV?], Rs?, R).
match_sgn(_, _, person(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, speech(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, undef, _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, nval(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, nfree(_), _, _, _, nomatch).

% A value argument num(X) matches a value by equality (def:unobstructed, at
% a binding of its schema; def:binding-numbers): the number X matches the
% number equal to it, and the value variable X is sent to the value it meets,
% or matches it if the binding sends X to it already.  Where one side is a
% value of the introductory act (nfree), whose value its introduction
% chooses, the match holds where the two are equal, and records the
% equation (eqv), which unobstructed.glp puts to the values.
procedure match_num(Constant?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_num(X, V, S, E, R?) :- number(X?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    match_lit(X?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_num(X, V, S, E, R?) :- otherwise, ground(X?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, num(X?), F),
    match_nvar(F?, X?, V?, S?, E?, R).

procedure match_lit(Constant?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_lit(X, nval(N), S, E, R?) :- number(N?), ground(S?), ground(E?) | num_eq(X?, N?, S?, E?, R).
match_lit(X, nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nval(X?), nfree(Y?))|E?])).
match_lit(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure num_eq(Constant?, Constant?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
num_eq(X, N, S, E, match(S?, E?)) :- X? =:= N? | true.
num_eq(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure match_nvar(Found?, Constant?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_nvar(free, X, nval(N), S, E, match([bind(num(X?), nval(N?))|S?], E?)).
match_nvar(free, X, nfree(Y), S, E, match([bind(num(X?), nfree(Y?))|S?], E?)).
match_nvar(bound(W), _, V, S, E, R?) :- ground(W?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    num_same(W?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_nvar(_, _, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure num_same(Val?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
num_same(nval(M), nval(N), S, E, R?) :- number(M?), number(N?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    num_eq(M?, N?, S?, E?, R).
num_same(nfree(Z), nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, E?)) :- Z? =?= Y? | true.
num_same(nval(M), nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nval(M?), nfree(Y?))|E?])).
num_same(nfree(Z), nval(N), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nfree(Z?), nval(N?))|E?])).
num_same(nfree(Z), nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nfree(Z?), nfree(Y?))|E?])) :-
    otherwise | true.
num_same(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure match_one(Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_one(sgn(Y, J), V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(Y?), integer(J?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_sgn(Y?, J?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).
match_one(num(X), V, S, E, _, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    match_num(X?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_one(A, V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    otherwise, ground(A?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, A?, F),
    match_one1(F?, A?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).

procedure match_rest(MatchRes?, Args?, Vals?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_rest(nomatch, _, _, _, nomatch).
match_rest(match(S, E), As, Vs, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(As?), ground(Vs?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_args(As?, Vs?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).

procedure match_args(Args?, Vals?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_args([], [], S, E, _, match(S?, E?)).
match_args([], [_|_], _, _, _, nomatch).
match_args([_|_], [], _, _, _, nomatch).
match_args([A|As], [V|Vs], S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(A?), ground(V?), ground(As?), ground(Vs?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_one(A?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R1),
    match_rest(R1?, As?, Vs?, Rs?, R).

% match_atom(Psi, G, Rs, S, E, R): the match of Psi against G extending the
% binding S and the equations E.
procedure match_atom(Atom?, GAtom?, RoleSpecs?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_atom(atom(P, As), gatom(Q, Vs), Rs, S, E, R?) :-
    P? =?= Q?, ground(As?), ground(Vs?), ground(Rs?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    match_args(As?, Vs?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).
match_atom(atom(_, _), gatom(_, _), _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

% A positive whole number, the value of a multiplicity (def:numbers,
% def:binding-numbers).
procedure pos_whole(Constant?, Ans).
pos_whole(X, yes) :- number(X?), X? >= 1, X? =:= floor(X?) | true.
pos_whole(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The variables of a schema
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure atoms_args(Atoms?, Args?, Args).
atoms_args([], T, T?).
atoms_args([atom(_, As)|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(Xs?), ground(T?) |
    atoms_args(Xs?, T?, R1),
    args_app(As?, R1?, R).

procedure rolespecs_args(RoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
rolespecs_args([], T, T?).
rolespecs_args([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    rs_add(RS?, P),
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    rs_keep(RS?, K),
    rs_forb(RS?, N),
    rolespecs_args(Rs?, T?, R1),
    atoms_args(N?, R1?, R2),
    atoms_args(K?, R2?, R3),
    atoms_args(M?, R3?, R4),
    atoms_args(P?, R4?, R).

procedure schema_args(Schema?, Args).
schema_args(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    rolespecs_args(Rs?, [], R).

% The party and speech-act variables a name term carries (def:role).
procedure nt_pvars(NameTerm?, Args).
nt_pvars(own(_), []).
nt_pvars(own_var(X), [pvar(X?)]).
nt_pvars(ext(S, _), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_pvars(S?, R).
nt_pvars(ext_any(S), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_pvars(S?, R).

procedure nt_svars(NameTerm?, Args).
nt_svars(own(_), []).
nt_svars(own_var(_), []).
nt_svars(ext(S, Y), R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Y?) |
    nt_svars(S?, R1),
    args_app(R1?, [svar(Y?)], R).
% The wildcard in place of the speech-act variable of Sigma.* is no variable.
nt_svars(ext_any(S), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_svars(S?, R).

% A signed term sgn(y, pi) carries the speech-act variable y and no party
% variable (def:schema).
procedure filter_pvars(Args?, Args).
filter_pvars([], []).
filter_pvars([pvar(X)|As], [pvar(X?)|R?]) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([role(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([svar(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([sgn(_, _)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([num(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([any|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([nterm(S)|As], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(As?) |
    nt_pvars(S?, Ps),
    filter_pvars(As?, R1),
    args_app(Ps?, R1?, R).

procedure filter_svars(Args?, Args).
filter_svars([], []).
filter_svars([svar(X)|As], [svar(X?)|R?]) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([role(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([pvar(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([sgn(Y, _)|As], [svar(Y?)|R?]) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([num(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([any|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([nterm(S)|As], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(As?) |
    nt_svars(S?, Ss),
    filter_svars(As?, R1),
    args_app(Ss?, R1?, R).

% The value variables among arguments: num(X) with X a name, a number being
% no variable (GSC, Section 3.2).
procedure filter_nvars(Args?, Args).
filter_nvars([], []).
filter_nvars([num(X)|As], R?) :- number(X?), ground(As?) | filter_nvars(As?, R).
filter_nvars([num(X)|As], [num(X?)|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(X?), ground(As?) |
    filter_nvars(As?, R).
filter_nvars([A|As], R?) :- otherwise, ground(A?), ground(As?) | filter_nvars(As?, R).

procedure schema_pvars(Schema?, Args).
schema_pvars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    filter_pvars(As?, Ps),
    args_dedup(Ps?, R).

procedure schema_svars(Schema?, Args).
schema_svars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    filter_svars(As?, Ss),
    args_dedup(Ss?, R).

% role_args(I, K, R): role(I) .. role(K).
procedure role_args(Integer?, Integer?, Args).
role_args(I, K, []) :- I? > K? | true.
role_args(I, K, [role(I?)|R?]) :- I? =< K?, integer(I?), integer(K?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    role_args(I1?, K?, R).

% Every variable of a schema: its roles, then its party and speech-act
% variables in order of first occurrence.
procedure schema_vars(Schema?, Args).
schema_vars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    roles_len(Rs?, K),
    role_args(1, K?, RA),
    schema_pvars(Sc?, PV),
    schema_svars(Sc?, SV),
    args_app(SV?, [], SV1),
    args_app(PV?, SV1?, PS),
    args_app(RA?, PS?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Completing a partial substitution with fresh names
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A match constrains only the variables it meets.  The rest take names no
% other binding in play uses: clause 2 of def:unobstructed excuses a binding
% that sends a role to the other party, and a variable the match left free can
% be sent elsewhere, so the fresh completion is the binding that decides it.

procedure fresh_val(Arg?, Integer?, Val).
fresh_val(role(_), N, person(N?)).
fresh_val(pvar(_), N, person(N?)).
fresh_val(svar(_), N, speech(N?)).
fresh_val(nterm(_), _, undef).
fresh_val(sgn(_, _), _, undef).
fresh_val(num(X), _, nfree(X?)).
fresh_val(any, _, undef).

procedure complete1(Found?, Arg?, Args?, Subst?, Integer?, Subst).
complete1(bound(_), _, As, S, N, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    complete_vars(As?, S?, N?, R).
complete1(free, A, As, S, N, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    fresh_val(A?, N?, V),
    N1 := N? + 1,
    complete_vars(As?, [bind(A?, V?)|S?], N1?, R).

procedure complete_vars(Args?, Subst?, Integer?, Subst).
complete_vars([], S, _, S?).
complete_vars([A|As], S, N, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, A?, F),
    complete1(F?, A?, As?, S?, N?, R).

procedure complete(Schema?, Subst?, Integer?, Subst).
complete(Sc, S, N, R?) :- ground(Sc?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    schema_vars(Sc?, Vs),
    complete_vars(Vs?, S?, N?, R).

% The first name index no binding of the introductory act uses: person(0) and
% person(1) are its two people and speech(0)..speech(m-1) its speech acts.
procedure fresh_base(Schema?, Integer).
fresh_base(Sc, N?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_svars(Sc?, SV),
    args_len(SV?, M),
    N := M? + 2.

procedure args_len(Args?, Integer).
args_len([], 0).
args_len([_|As], N?) :- args_len(As?, M), N := M? + 1.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Atoms a role requires (def:schema: the atoms =(i) and -(i))
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% atoms_witness(Phis, U, E, R): some atom of Phis has its predicate in E and U
% among its arguments.
procedure atoms_witness1(Ans?, Atoms?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
atoms_witness1(yes, _, _, _, yes).
atoms_witness1(no, Xs, U, E, R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    atoms_witness(Xs?, U?, E?, R).

procedure atoms_witness(Atoms?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
atoms_witness([], _, _, no).
atoms_witness([atom(Q, As)|Xs], U, E, R?) :-
    ground(Q?), ground(As?), ground(Xs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    pred_member(Q?, E?, A1),
    args_member(As?, U?, A2),
    both_yes(A1?, A2?, B),
    atoms_witness1(B?, Xs?, U?, E?, R).

% req_names(Role, U, E, R): the role requires an atom with predicate in E and
% U among its arguments.
procedure req_names(RoleSpec?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
req_names(RS, U, E, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    rs_del(RS?, M),
    rs_keep(RS?, K),
    atoms_witness(M?, U?, E?, A1),
    atoms_witness(K?, U?, E?, A2),
    or_yes(A1?, A2?, R).

procedure any_req_names1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
any_req_names1(yes, _, _, _, yes).
any_req_names1(no, Rs, U, E, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    any_req_names(Rs?, U?, E?, R).

procedure any_req_names(RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
any_req_names([], _, _, no).
any_req_names([RS|Rs], U, E, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    req_names(RS?, U?, E?, A),
    any_req_names1(A?, Rs?, U?, E?, R).

% req_occurs(Role, Y, R): the speech-act variable Y occurs in an atom the role
% requires, whatever its predicate -- as an argument or inside a name-term
% argument (def:grounded: "occurs in no atom required
% at a role").
procedure req_occurs(RoleSpec?, Arg?, Ans).
req_occurs(RS, Y, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Y?) |
    rs_req(RS?, Req),
    atoms_args(Req?, [], As),
    filter_svars(As?, SV),
    args_member(SV?, Y?, R).

procedure any_req_occurs1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Ans).
any_req_occurs1(yes, _, _, yes).
any_req_occurs1(no, Rs, Y, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(Y?) |
    any_req_occurs(Rs?, Y?, R).

procedure any_req_occurs(RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Ans).
any_req_occurs([], _, no).
any_req_occurs([RS|Rs], Y, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(Y?) |
    req_occurs(RS?, Y?, A),
    any_req_occurs1(A?, Rs?, Y?, R).

% nth_rs(Rs, I, R): the I-th role of a schema, counting from one.  The empty
% case is out of range and cannot arise; it answers with a role that requires
% nothing, so that a caller reports a fault rather than passing.
procedure nth_rs(RoleSpecs?, Integer?, RoleSpec).
nth_rs([], _, rs(unguarded, [], [], [], [])).
nth_rs([X|_], I, X?) :- I? =:= 1 | true.
nth_rs([_|Xs], I, R?) :- I? > 1, integer(I?), ground(Xs?) |
    I1 := I? - 1,
    nth_rs(Xs?, I1?, R).

procedure guard_marked(Guard?, Ans).
guard_marked(guarded, yes).
guard_marked(unguarded, no).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Reflexive predicates (GAI's appendix "Contracts with Wards")
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% The predicates a contract declares reflexive, and its schemas.
procedure decl_reflexive(Declared?, Preds).
decl_reflexive([], []).
decl_reflexive([_|_], []).
decl_reflexive(reflexive(Rf, _), Rf?).

procedure decl_schemas(Declared?, Contract).
decl_schemas([], []).
decl_schemas([S|Ss], [S?|Ss?]).
decl_schemas(reflexive(_, C), C?).

% own_reflexive(Phi, I, Rf, R): Phi is the atom of a reflexive predicate, one
% of Rf, naming the role I.
procedure own_reflexive(Atom?, Integer?, Preds?, Ans).
own_reflexive(atom(P, [role(J)]), I, Rf, R?) :-
    J? =:= I?, ground(P?), ground(Rf?) |
    pred_member(P?, Rf?, R).
own_reflexive(atom(_, _), _, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% refl_keep(Phis, I, Rf, W, R): the atoms of Phis for which own_reflexive
% answers W, in order: W = yes keeps the atoms of a reflexive predicate naming
% the role I, and W = no the others.
procedure refl_keep1(Ans?, Ans?, Atom?, Atoms?, Integer?, Preds?, Atoms).
refl_keep1(B, W, A, Xs, I, Rf, [A?|R?]) :-
    B? =?= W?, ground(Xs?), integer(I?), ground(Rf?) |
    refl_keep(Xs?, I?, Rf?, W?, R).
refl_keep1(_, W, _, Xs, I, Rf, R?) :-
    otherwise, ground(W?), ground(Xs?), integer(I?), ground(Rf?) |
    refl_keep(Xs?, I?, Rf?, W?, R).

procedure refl_keep(Atoms?, Integer?, Preds?, Ans?, Atoms).
refl_keep([], _, _, _, []).
refl_keep([A|Xs], I, Rf, W, R?) :-
    ground(A?), ground(Xs?), integer(I?), ground(Rf?), ground(W?) |
    own_reflexive(A?, I?, Rf?, B),
    refl_keep1(B?, W?, A?, Xs?, I?, Rf?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Roles, bases and name terms (def:role)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A schema is written schema(Name, Vars, Roles), or cschema(Name, Vars, [],
% Roles); a role is written rs(...) where it is an agent role and
% crs(Kind, ...) where it is a listed role.  The accessors below read
% either.

procedure sch_name(Schema?, Constant).
sch_name(schema(Nm, _, _), Nm?).
sch_name(cschema(Nm, _, _, _), Nm?).

% The variables of a schema, in the order of its head.
procedure sch_vars(Schema?, Args).
sch_vars(schema(_, Vs, _), Vs?).
sch_vars(cschema(_, Vs, _, _), Vs?).

procedure sch_roles(Schema?, RoleSpecs).
sch_roles(schema(_, _, Rs), Rs?).
sch_roles(cschema(_, _, _, Rs), Rs?).

procedure rs_guard(RoleSpec?, Guard).
rs_guard(rs(G, _, _, _, _), G?).
rs_guard(crs(_, G, _, _, _, _), G?).

procedure rs_add(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_add(rs(_, P, _, _, _), P?).
rs_add(crs(_, _, P, _, _, _), P?).

% A role's atoms marked -, as the term form writes them: -(i), those with no
% wildcard, and *(i), its cleared atoms, those with one (def:schema, GSC
% 327e035).
procedure rs_marked_del(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_marked_del(rs(_, _, M, _, _), M?).
rs_marked_del(crs(_, _, _, M, _, _), M?).

% -(i): the atoms the role deletes, marked - with no wildcard.
procedure rs_del(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_del(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    atoms_cleared(M?, no, R).

% *(i): the role's cleared atoms, marked - with a wildcard.
procedure rs_clear(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_clear(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    atoms_cleared(M?, yes, R).

% Whether an atom carries the wildcard: among its arguments, or in place of
% the speech-act variable of a name term among them (def:schema).
procedure nt_wild(NameTerm?, Ans).
nt_wild(own(_), no).
nt_wild(own_var(_), no).
nt_wild(ext(S, _), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_wild(S?, R).
nt_wild(ext_any(_), yes).

procedure arg_wild(Arg?, Ans).
arg_wild(any, yes).
arg_wild(nterm(S), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_wild(S?, R).
arg_wild(A, no) :- otherwise, ground(A?) | true.

procedure args_wild1(Ans?, Args?, Ans).
args_wild1(yes, _, yes).
args_wild1(no, As, R?) :- ground(As?) | args_wild(As?, R).

procedure args_wild(Args?, Ans).
args_wild([], no).
args_wild([A|As], R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    arg_wild(A?, W),
    args_wild1(W?, As?, R).

procedure atom_wild(Atom?, Ans).
atom_wild(atom(_, As), R?) :- ground(As?) | args_wild(As?, R).

% atoms_cleared(Phis, W, R): the atoms of Phis carrying the wildcard (W = yes)
% or not carrying it (W = no), in order.
procedure atoms_cleared1(Ans?, Ans?, Atom?, Atoms?, Atoms).
atoms_cleared1(B, W, A, Xs, [A?|R?]) :- B? =?= W?, ground(Xs?) |
    atoms_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).
atoms_cleared1(_, W, _, Xs, R?) :- otherwise, ground(W?), ground(Xs?) |
    atoms_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).

procedure atoms_cleared(Atoms?, Ans?, Atoms).
atoms_cleared([], _, []).
atoms_cleared([A|Xs], W, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Xs?), ground(W?) |
    atom_wild(A?, B),
    atoms_cleared1(B?, W?, A?, Xs?, R).

% matches_cleared(Phi, Psi, R): the atom Phi is obtained from the cleared atom
% Psi by replacing its wildcards, each by an argument, a speech-act variable
% where the wildcard is in a name term (def:schema, def:binding).
procedure nt_wild_match(NameTerm?, NameTerm?, Ans).
nt_wild_match(ext_any(S), ext(T, _), R?) :- ground(S?), ground(T?) |
    nt_wild_match(S?, T?, R).
nt_wild_match(ext(S, Y), ext(T, Z), R?) :- Y? =?= Z?, ground(S?), ground(T?) |
    nt_wild_match(S?, T?, R).
nt_wild_match(S, T, yes) :- otherwise, S? =?= T? | true.
nt_wild_match(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure arg_wild_match(Arg?, Arg?, Ans).
arg_wild_match(any, _, yes).
arg_wild_match(nterm(S), nterm(T), R?) :- ground(S?), ground(T?) |
    nt_wild_match(S?, T?, R).
arg_wild_match(A, B, yes) :- otherwise, A? =?= B? | true.
arg_wild_match(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure args_wild_match1(Ans?, Args?, Args?, Ans).
args_wild_match1(no, _, _, no).
args_wild_match1(yes, Ps, As, R?) :- ground(Ps?), ground(As?) |
    args_wild_match(Ps?, As?, R).

procedure args_wild_match(Args?, Args?, Ans).
args_wild_match([], [], yes).
args_wild_match([P|Ps], [A|As], R?) :- ground(P?), ground(Ps?), ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    arg_wild_match(P?, A?, M),
    args_wild_match1(M?, Ps?, As?, R).
args_wild_match(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure matches_cleared(Atom?, Atom?, Ans).
matches_cleared(atom(P, As), atom(Q, Bs), R?) :-
    P? =?= Q?, ground(As?), ground(Bs?) |
    args_wild_match(Bs?, As?, R).
matches_cleared(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% matches_some_cleared(Phi, Psis, R): Phi is obtained from some atom of Psis.
procedure matches_some1(Ans?, Atom?, Atoms?, Ans).
matches_some1(yes, _, _, yes).
matches_some1(no, A, Cs, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Cs?) | matches_some_cleared(A?, Cs?, R).

procedure matches_some_cleared(Atom?, Atoms?, Ans).
matches_some_cleared(_, [], no).
matches_some_cleared(A, [C|Cs], R?) :- ground(A?), ground(C?), ground(Cs?) |
    matches_cleared(A?, C?, M),
    matches_some1(M?, A?, Cs?, R).

procedure rs_keep(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_keep(rs(_, _, _, K, _), K?).
rs_keep(crs(_, _, _, _, K, _), K?).

procedure rs_forb(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_forb(rs(_, _, _, _, N), N?).
rs_forb(crs(_, _, _, _, _, N), N?).

% The atoms a role requires: =(i) u -(i) (def:schema), a cleared atom
% requiring none.
procedure rs_req(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_req(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_del(RS?, M),
    rs_keep(RS?, K),
    atoms_app(K?, M?, R).

procedure is_party_role(RoleSpec?, Ans).
is_party_role(rs(_, _, _, _, _), yes).
is_party_role(crs(_, _, _, _, _, _), no).

procedure is_guarding(RoleSpec?, Ans).
is_guarding(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_guard(RS?, G),
    guard_marked(G?, R).

% A reading role (def:schema, GSC 0380a8a): a role that is not a guarding
% role and has +(i) u -(i) empty, -(i) the atoms marked - with no wildcard,
% so a cleared atom is no change.
procedure reading_role(RoleSpec?, Ans).
reading_role(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    is_guarding(RS?, G),
    rs_add(RS?, P),
    rs_del(RS?, M),
    reading_role1(G?, P?, M?, R).

procedure reading_role1(Ans?, Atoms?, Atoms?, Ans).
reading_role1(no, [], [], yes).
reading_role1(_, _, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% Some role among the indices Js is no reading role.  Clause 2 of
% def:unobstructed asks it of the roles a binding sends the other agent to.
procedure some_not_reading(Ints?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
some_not_reading([], _, no).
some_not_reading([J|Js], Rs, R?) :- integer(J?), ground(Js?), ground(Rs?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, J?, RS),
    reading_role(RS?, A),
    some_not_reading1(A?, Js?, Rs?, R).

procedure some_not_reading1(Ans?, Ints?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
some_not_reading1(no, _, _, yes).
some_not_reading1(yes, Js, Rs, R?) :- ground(Js?), ground(Rs?) |
    some_not_reading(Js?, Rs?, R).

procedure nt_base(NameTerm?, Base).
nt_base(own(I), b_role(I?)).
nt_base(own_var(X), b_pvar(X?)).
nt_base(ext(S, _), B?) :- ground(S?) | nt_base(S?, B).
% <pi>.* in a cleared atom is a name term with its speech-act variable
% replaced by the wildcard (def:schema), its base that of <pi>.
nt_base(ext_any(S), B?) :- ground(S?) | nt_base(S?, B).

procedure arg_base(Arg?, Base).
arg_base(role(I), b_role(I?)).
arg_base(pvar(X), b_pvar(X?)).
arg_base(svar(X), b_svar(X?)).
arg_base(nterm(S), B?) :- ground(S?) | nt_base(S?, B).
% A signed term sgn(y, pi) counts as the two arguments y and pi
% (def:grounded): this is the base of pi, an agent role, and
% filter_svars gives y.
arg_base(sgn(_, J), b_role(J?)).
arg_base(num(_), b_num).
arg_base(any, b_any).

procedure role_base(RoleSpec?, Integer?, Base).
role_base(rs(_, _, _, _, _), I, b_role(I?)).
% The base of a listed role pi[rho(*, u_2, ..., u_r)] is the agent role pi
% (def:role, GSC 8064cfb).
role_base(crs(listed(I, _, _), _, _, _, _, _), _, b_role(I?)).

procedure nth_base(RoleSpecs?, Integer?, Base).
nth_base(Rs, I, B?) :- ground(Rs?), integer(I?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, I?, RS),
    role_base(RS?, I?, B).

% The bases of arguments (def:grounded at GSC 1934846): an agent role, an
% agent variable and a name term have one; a value and a speech-act variable
% have none, a value naming no agent (the appendix "Values in Speech-Act Schemas").
procedure args_bases(Args?, Bases?, Bases).
args_bases([], T, T?).
args_bases([num(_)|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([svar(_)|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([any|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([A|As], T, [B?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    arg_base(A?, B),
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).

% The bases of the arguments of the atoms of Phi_E among a list of atoms
% (def:grounded, def:volition).
procedure phi_bases1(Ans?, Args?, Bases?, Bases).
phi_bases1(no, _, T, T?).
phi_bases1(yes, As, T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) | args_bases(As?, T?, R).

procedure phi_bases(Atoms?, Preds?, Bases?, Bases).
phi_bases([], _, T, T?).
phi_bases([atom(Q, As)|Xs], E, T, R?) :-
    ground(Q?), ground(As?), ground(Xs?), ground(E?), ground(T?) |
    pred_member(Q?, E?, M),
    phi_bases(Xs?, E?, T?, R1),
    phi_bases1(M?, As?, R1?, R).

% The arguments u_2, ..., u_r of a listed role pi[rho(*, u_2, ..., u_r)],
% arguments of its schema (def:role); an agent role has none.
procedure rs_kind_args(RoleSpec?, Args).
rs_kind_args(rs(_, _, _, _, _), []).
rs_kind_args(crs(listed(_, _, As), _, _, _, _, _), As?).

procedure rolespecs_kind_args(RoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
rolespecs_kind_args([], T, T?).
rolespecs_kind_args([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    rs_kind_args(RS?, As),
    rolespecs_kind_args(Rs?, T?, R1),
    args_app(As?, R1?, R).


% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The name terms of a schema (def:role)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Those among the arguments of its listed roles, and those among the
% arguments of its atoms, in that order.

procedure nts_of_args(Args?, NameTerms?, NameTerms).
nts_of_args([], T, T?).
nts_of_args([nterm(S)|As], T, [S?|R?]) :- ground(S?), ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    nts_of_args(As?, T?, R).
nts_of_args([A|As], T, R?) :- otherwise, ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    nts_of_args(As?, T?, R).

procedure nts_of_roles(RoleSpecs?, NameTerms?, NameTerms).
nts_of_roles([], T, T?).
nts_of_roles([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    rs_kind_args(RS?, KA),
    nts_of_roles(Rs?, T?, R1),
    nts_of_args(KA?, R1?, R).

procedure sch_nts(Schema?, NameTerms).
sch_nts(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    nts_of_roles(Rs?, [], N1),
    nts_of_args(As?, N1?, R).

% The agent and speech-act variables occurring in a schema: in its atoms,
% within their name terms and signed terms, and in the arguments of its
% listed roles.
procedure sch_occ_vars1(Args?, Args).
sch_occ_vars1(All, R?) :- ground(All?) |
    filter_pvars(All?, Ps),
    filter_svars(All?, Ss),
    args_app(Ps?, Ss?, PS),
    args_dedup(PS?, R).

procedure sch_occ_vars(Schema?, Args).
sch_occ_vars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    sch_occ_vars2(Rs?, As?, R).

procedure sch_occ_vars2(RoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
sch_occ_vars2(Rs, As, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(As?) |
    rolespecs_kind_args(Rs?, [], KAs),
    args_app(As?, KAs?, All),
    sch_occ_vars1(All?, R).

procedure nts_empty(NameTerms?, Ans).
nts_empty([], yes).
nts_empty([_|_], no).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The contract as written, with numbers (GSC, def:numbers)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A contract is read as written, of the types N..., and its plain form is
% the one traceable provenance and volition are decided on: each
% multiplicity dropped, leaving its atom, and the constraint of an nschema
% dropped, leaving a schema with the same name, variables and roles.  A
% number names no agent, so those conditions do not concern numbers (GSC,
% Section 3.2): a value argument stays in its atom, where it names no one.
% def:unobstructed asks that an atom be added at a binding of a schema, which
% satisfies its constraint, and is decided on the contract as written
% (unobstructed.glp), the number of a value argument matched by equality
% (apply_arg, match_num).  The form of a schema is decided on the plain form
% too, an atom with a multiplicity being an atom added or deleted
% (def:schema), and the head and the numbers on the contract as written
% (check.glp).

procedure plain_mult(Mult?, Atom).
plain_mult(atom(P, As), atom(P?, As?)).
plain_mult(times(_, A), A?).

procedure plain_mults(Mults?, Atoms).
plain_mults([], []).
plain_mults([M|Ms], [A?|R?]) :- ground(M?), ground(Ms?) |
    plain_mult(M?, A),
    plain_mults(Ms?, R).

procedure plain_role(NRoleSpec?, RoleSpec).
plain_role(rs(G, P, M, K, N), rs(G?, P1?, M1?, K1?, N1?)) :-
    ground(P?), ground(M?), ground(K?), ground(N?) |
    plain_mults(P?, P1),
    plain_mults(M?, M1),
    plain_mults(K?, K1),
    plain_mults(N?, N1).
plain_role(crs(Kd, G, P, M, K, N), crs(Kd?, G?, P1?, M1?, K1?, N1?)) :-
    ground(P?), ground(M?), ground(K?), ground(N?) |
    plain_mults(P?, P1),
    plain_mults(M?, M1),
    plain_mults(K?, K1),
    plain_mults(N?, N1).

procedure plain_roles(NRoleSpecs?, RoleSpecs).
plain_roles([], []).
plain_roles([RS|Rs], [R1?|R?]) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?) |
    plain_role(RS?, R1),
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).

procedure plain_schema(NSchema?, Schema).
plain_schema(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, R?)) :- ground(Rs?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).
plain_schema(cschema(Nm, Vs, Nl, Rs), cschema(Nm?, Vs?, Nl?, R?)) :- ground(Rs?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).
plain_schema(nschema(Nm, Vs, _, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, R?)) :- ground(Rs?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).

procedure plain_contract(NContract?, Contract).
plain_contract([], []).
plain_contract([S|Ss], [P?|R?]) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    plain_schema(S?, P),
    plain_contract(Ss?, R).

procedure plain_decl(NDeclared?, Declared).
plain_decl([], []).
plain_decl([S|Ss], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | plain_contract([S?|Ss?], R).
plain_decl(reflexive(Rf, C), reflexive(Rf?, R?)) :- ground(C?) | plain_contract(C?, R).

% The schemas of a contract as written, and the predicates it declares
% reflexive.
procedure ndecl_schemas(NDeclared?, NContract).
ndecl_schemas([], []).
ndecl_schemas([S|Ss], [S?|Ss?]).
ndecl_schemas(reflexive(_, C), C?).

procedure ndecl_reflexive(NDeclared?, Preds).
ndecl_reflexive([], []).
ndecl_reflexive([_|_], []).
ndecl_reflexive(reflexive(Rf, _), Rf?).

% num_ctx(NSc, nc(C, Pw)): the constraint of a schema as written, true where
% it has none, and the value variables it uses as multiplicities.
procedure num_ctx(NSchema?, NumCtx).
num_ctx(NSc, nc(C?, Pw?)) :- ground(NSc?) |
    nsch_constraint(NSc?, C),
    nsch_roles(NSc?, Rs),
    nroles_margs(Rs?, [], Ms),
    filter_nvars(Ms?, Ms1),
    args_dedup(Ms1?, Pw).

% The parts of a schema as written.  The constraint of a schema with none is
% true.
procedure nsch_name(NSchema?, Constant).
nsch_name(schema(Nm, _, _), Nm?).
nsch_name(cschema(Nm, _, _, _), Nm?).
nsch_name(nschema(Nm, _, _, _), Nm?).

procedure nsch_vars(NSchema?, Args).
nsch_vars(schema(_, Vs, _), Vs?).
nsch_vars(cschema(_, Vs, _, _), Vs?).
nsch_vars(nschema(_, Vs, _, _), Vs?).

procedure nsch_roles(NSchema?, NRoleSpecs).
nsch_roles(schema(_, _, Rs), Rs?).
nsch_roles(cschema(_, _, _, Rs), Rs?).
nsch_roles(nschema(_, _, _, Rs), Rs?).

procedure nsch_constraint(NSchema?, Constraint).
nsch_constraint(schema(_, _, _), true).
nsch_constraint(cschema(_, _, _, _), true).
nsch_constraint(nschema(_, _, C, _), C?).

procedure nrs_guard(NRoleSpec?, Guard).
nrs_guard(rs(G, _, _, _, _), G?).
nrs_guard(crs(_, G, _, _, _, _), G?).

procedure nrs_add(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_add(rs(_, P, _, _, _), P?).
nrs_add(crs(_, _, P, _, _, _), P?).

% A role's atoms marked -, as written: -(i), those with no wildcard, and
% *(i), its cleared atoms (def:schema, GSC 327e035).
procedure nrs_marked_del(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_marked_del(rs(_, _, M, _, _), M?).
nrs_marked_del(crs(_, _, _, M, _, _), M?).

procedure nrs_del(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_del(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    mults_cleared(M?, no, R).

procedure nrs_clear(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_clear(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    mults_cleared(M?, yes, R).

procedure mult_wild(Mult?, Ans).
mult_wild(atom(P, As), R?) :- ground(P?), ground(As?) | atom_wild(atom(P?, As?), R).
mult_wild(times(_, A), R?) :- ground(A?) | atom_wild(A?, R).

procedure mults_cleared1(Ans?, Ans?, Mult?, Mults?, Mults).
mults_cleared1(B, W, A, Xs, [A?|R?]) :- B? =?= W?, ground(Xs?) |
    mults_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).
mults_cleared1(_, W, _, Xs, R?) :- otherwise, ground(W?), ground(Xs?) |
    mults_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).

procedure mults_cleared(Mults?, Ans?, Mults).
mults_cleared([], _, []).
mults_cleared([A|Xs], W, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Xs?), ground(W?) |
    mult_wild(A?, B),
    mults_cleared1(B?, W?, A?, Xs?, R).

procedure nrs_keep(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_keep(rs(_, _, _, K, _), K?).
nrs_keep(crs(_, _, _, _, K, _), K?).

procedure nrs_forb(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_forb(rs(_, _, _, _, N), N?).
nrs_forb(crs(_, _, _, _, _, N), N?).

procedure mults_app(Mults?, Mults?, Mults).
mults_app([], T, T?).
mults_app([M|Ms], T, [M?|R?]) :- mults_app(Ms?, T?, R).

% The atoms a role requires, as written: =(i) u -(i).
procedure nrs_req(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_req(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_del(RS?, M),
    nrs_keep(RS?, K),
    mults_app(K?, M?, R).

procedure n_is_guarding(NRoleSpec?, Ans).
n_is_guarding(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_guard(RS?, G),
    guard_marked(G?, R).

% The arguments of a constraint's linear equalities and inequalities, and the
% multiplicities among a multiset as written.  A signing condition is over an
% agent and a speech act, not over values, and gives none.
procedure constraint_args(Constraint?, Args?, Args).
constraint_args(true, T, T?).
constraint_args(and(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_args(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_args(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_args(eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(le(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(lt(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(ge(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(gt(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(succ(X, Y), T, [X?, Y?|T?]).
constraint_args(or(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_args(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_args(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_args(signed(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_args(unsigned(_, _), T, T?).

% The agent and speech-act variables among the arguments of signing
% conditions.
procedure sargs_vars(Args?, Args).
sargs_vars(Ss, R?) :- ground(Ss?) |
    filter_pvars(Ss?, Ps),
    filter_svars(Ss?, Ys),
    args_app(Ps?, Ys?, R).

% The arguments of a constraint's signing conditions, u and y of each
% signed(u, y) and unsigned(u, y) (def:numbers, GSC 10fcc92).
procedure constraint_sargs(Constraint?, Args?, Args).
constraint_sargs(true, T, T?).
constraint_sargs(and(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_sargs(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_sargs(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_sargs(or(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_sargs(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_sargs(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_sargs(eq(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(le(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(lt(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(ge(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(gt(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(succ(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(signed(U, Y), T, [U?, Y?|T?]).
constraint_sargs(unsigned(U, Y), T, [U?, Y?|T?]).

% The arguments an expression is made of.
procedure expr_args(Expr?, Args?, Args).
expr_args(plus(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
expr_args(minus(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
expr_args(mul(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
expr_args(num(X), T, [num(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(role(I), T, [role(I?)|T?]).
expr_args(pvar(X), T, [pvar(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(svar(X), T, [svar(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(nterm(N), T, [nterm(N?)|T?]).
expr_args(sgn(Y, J), T, [sgn(Y?, J?)|T?]).
expr_args(any, T, [any|T?]).

procedure exprs_args(Exprs?, Args?, Args).
exprs_args([], T, T?).
exprs_args([X|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Xs?), ground(T?) |
    exprs_args(Xs?, T?, R1),
    expr_args(X?, R1?, R).

procedure mults_margs(Mults?, Args?, Args).
mults_margs([], T, T?).
mults_margs([atom(_, _)|Ms], T, R?) :- ground(Ms?), ground(T?) | mults_margs(Ms?, T?, R).
mults_margs([times(K, _)|Ms], T, [K?|R?]) :- ground(Ms?), ground(T?) | mults_margs(Ms?, T?, R).

procedure nroles_margs(NRoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
nroles_margs([], T, T?).
nroles_margs([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    nrs_add(RS?, P),
    nrs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    nrs_keep(RS?, K),
    nrs_forb(RS?, N),
    nroles_margs(Rs?, T?, R1),
    mults_margs(N?, R1?, R2),
    mults_margs(K?, R2?, R3),
    mults_margs(M?, R3?, R4),
    mults_margs(P?, R4?, R).

% The variables occurring in a schema as written: its agent and speech-act
% variables (sch_occ_vars of its plain form), then those of its signing
% conditions that its atoms do not carry, then its value variables, in its
% atoms, its multiplicities and its constraint.
procedure nsch_occ_vars(NSchema?, Args).
nsch_occ_vars(NSc, R?) :- ground(NSc?) |
    plain_schema(NSc?, Sc),
    nsch_roles(NSc?, NRs),
    nsch_constraint(NSc?, Cn),
    nsch_occ_vars1(Sc?, NRs?, Cn?, R).

procedure nsch_occ_vars1(Schema?, NRoleSpecs?, Constraint?, Args).
nsch_occ_vars1(Sc, NRs, Cn, R?) :- ground(Sc?), ground(NRs?), ground(Cn?) |
    sch_occ_vars(Sc?, PS0),
    constraint_sargs(Cn?, [], Ss),
    sargs_vars(Ss?, SV),
    args_app(PS0?, SV?, PSV),
    args_dedup(PSV?, PS),
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    nroles_margs(NRs?, [], Ms),
    constraint_args(Cn?, [], Cs),
    args_app(Ms?, Cs?, MC),
    args_app(As?, MC?, All),
    filter_nvars(All?, Ns),
    args_dedup(Ns?, Ns1),
    args_app(PS?, Ns1?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A contract with community roles
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A contract with a listed role, a name term or a schema written cschema has
% community roles.  def:syntactically-grassroots is one definition for every
% contract (GSC ac7ad63), and the distinction is the wards': GAI's appendix
% "Contracts with Wards" is written over the schemas of agent roles with no
% name term, and CSSN's def:sg-wards over those of an agent-named contract
% (check.glp; wards/).

procedure roles_community1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
roles_community1(yes, _, yes).
roles_community1(no, Rs, R?) :- ground(Rs?) | roles_community(Rs?, R).

procedure roles_community(RoleSpecs?, Ans).
roles_community([], no).
roles_community([RS|Rs], R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?) |
    is_party_role(RS?, P),
    flip(P?, A),
    roles_community1(A?, Rs?, R).

procedure sch_community(Schema?, Ans).
sch_community(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), R?) :- ground(Nm?), ground(Vs?), ground(Rs?) |
    roles_community(Rs?, A1),
    sch_nts(schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?), Ns),
    nts_empty(Ns?, A2),
    flip(A2?, A3),
    or_yes(A1?, A3?, R).
sch_community(cschema(_, _, _, _), yes).

procedure has_community1(Ans?, Contract?, Ans).
has_community1(yes, _, yes).
has_community1(no, Ss, R?) :- ground(Ss?) | has_community(Ss?, R).

procedure has_community(Contract?, Ans).
has_community([], no).
has_community([S|Ss], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    sch_community(S?, A),
    has_community1(A?, Ss?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The base of a name term (def:role)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A name term of a schema is <pi> for an agent role pi of it, or sigma.y for
% a name term sigma of it (def:role), so its base is an agent role of that
% schema; check.glp refuses a contract with a name term whose base is not
% (name_term_base).  A contract every name term of which is so is
% agent-named in the sense of CSSN's def:agent-named, which def:sg-wards
% asks of a contract with wards and listed roles.

% The base B is an agent role of the schema whose roles are Rs.
procedure base_agent_role1(Integer?, Integer?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
base_agent_role1(I, K, Rs, R?) :- I? >= 1, I? =< K?, ground(Rs?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, I?, RS),
    is_party_role(RS?, R).
base_agent_role1(_, _, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure base_agent_role(Base?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
base_agent_role(b_role(I), Rs, R?) :- integer(I?), ground(Rs?) |
    roles_len(Rs?, K),
    base_agent_role1(I?, K?, Rs?, R).
base_agent_role(B, _, no) :- otherwise, ground(B?) | true.

procedure nts_agent_based1(Ans?, NameTerms?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
nts_agent_based1(no, _, _, no).
nts_agent_based1(yes, Ns, Rs, R?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(Rs?) | nts_agent_based(Ns?, Rs?, R).

procedure nts_agent_based(NameTerms?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
nts_agent_based([], _, yes).
nts_agent_based([S|Ns], Rs, R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ns?), ground(Rs?) |
    nt_base(S?, B),
    base_agent_role(B?, Rs?, A),
    nts_agent_based1(A?, Ns?, Rs?, R).

procedure sch_agent_named(Schema?, Ans).
sch_agent_named(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    sch_nts(Sc?, Ns),
    nts_agent_based(Ns?, Rs?, R).

procedure agent_named1(Ans?, Contract?, Ans).
agent_named1(no, _, no).
agent_named1(yes, Ss, R?) :- ground(Ss?) | agent_named(Ss?, R).

procedure agent_named(Contract?, Ans).
agent_named([], yes).
agent_named([S|Ss], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    sch_agent_named(S?, A),
    agent_named1(A?, Ss?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Entry points
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% The directory's interface: each entry point is forwarded to the module that
% defines it (manual 19.6).  check.glp composes the three conjuncts of
% def:syntactically-grassroots.  A contract is given as a term, printed by
% contract_named/2 in a REPL session on its owner's file (contracts.glp, the
% header); contracts.glp holds the checker's fixtures, by name, and its
% variants of a contract, by name and the contract's term.

imported procedure check#check_env(NDeclared?, Preds?, Verdict).
exported procedure check(WDeclared?, Verdict).
check(C, V?) :- ground(C?) |
    read_faults(C?, F),
    check_read(F?, C?, V).

% A contract whose reading has faults is malformed, with them; one whose
% reading has none is decided on what it reads to.
procedure check_read(Faults?, WDeclared?, Verdict).
check_read([], C, V?) :- ground(C?) |
    unnamed(C?, D),
    env_preds(C?, Ev),
    check # check_env(D?, Ev?, V).
check_read([F|Fs], _, malformed([F?|Fs?])).

imported procedure check#check_named(Constant?, Verdict).
exported procedure check_named(Constant?, Verdict).
check_named(Nm, V?) :- check # check_named(Nm?, V).

imported procedure check#check_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Verdict).
exported procedure check_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Verdict).
check_variant(Nm, B, V?) :- check # check_variant(Nm?, B?, V).

imported procedure check#traceable_of(Constant?, Preds).
exported procedure traceable_of(Constant?, Preds).
traceable_of(Nm, E?) :- check # traceable_of(Nm?, E).

imported procedure check#traceable_preds(NDeclared?, Preds).
exported procedure traceable_preds(WDeclared?, Preds).
traceable_preds(D, E?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # traceable_preds(D0?, E).

imported procedure check#traceable_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Preds).
exported procedure traceable_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Preds).
traceable_variant(Nm, B, E?) :- check # traceable_variant(Nm?, B?, E).

% The introductory acts of a contract, for inspection (def:introduction,
% def:unobstructed): each unobstructed, or obstructed with its faults.
imported procedure check#intro_acts(NDeclared?, IntroActs).
exported procedure intro_acts(WDeclared?, IntroActs).
intro_acts(D, A?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # intro_acts(D0?, A).

imported procedure check#intro_acts_variant(Constant?, WContract?, IntroActs).
exported procedure intro_acts_variant(Constant?, WContract?, IntroActs).
intro_acts_variant(Nm, B, A?) :- check # intro_acts_variant(Nm?, B?, A).

% The introduction with wards (GAI, "Contracts with Wards"), for inspection:
% what the search found, or that there is none; the guardianships for a set
% of marks; and the leaving marks for it, with each choice of a guardianship
% per mark.
imported procedure check#wards_of(Constant?, Wards).
exported procedure wards_of(Constant?, Wards).
wards_of(Nm, W?) :- check # wards_of(Nm?, W).

imported procedure check#wards(NDeclared?, Wards).
exported procedure wards(WDeclared?, Wards).
wards(D, W?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # wards(D0?, W).

imported procedure check#wards_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Wards).
exported procedure wards_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Wards).
wards_variant(Nm, B, W?) :- check # wards_variant(Nm?, B?, W).

imported procedure check#guardianships(NDeclared?, Preds?, Guardianships).
exported procedure guardianships(WDeclared?, Preds?, Guardianships).
guardianships(D, M, G?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # guardianships(D0?, M?, G).

% The atoms the relay acts of the introduction with wards require at their ward roles as atoms of h, by clause 2 of def:relay and by none of its other alternatives (GSC 410a440), of a contract given as a term.
imported procedure check#relay_h(NDeclared?, RelayHs).
exported procedure relay_h(WDeclared?, RelayHs).
relay_h(D, H?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # relay_h(D0?, H).

% The leaving marks of a contract for a set of marks (def:leaving), for each
% choice of a guardianship of each mark, of a contract given as a term and
% of a fixture by name.
imported procedure check#leaving(NDeclared?, Preds?, Leavings).
exported procedure leaving(WDeclared?, Preds?, Leavings).
leaving(D, M, L?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # leaving(D0?, M?, L).

imported procedure check#leaving_of(Constant?, Preds?, Leavings).
exported procedure leaving_of(Constant?, Preds?, Leavings).
leaving_of(Nm, M, L?) :- check # leaving_of(Nm?, M?, L).

imported procedure contracts#contract(Constant?, NDeclared).
exported procedure contract_named(Constant?, NDeclared).
contract_named(Nm, C?) :- contracts # contract(Nm?, C).

imported procedure contracts#variant(Constant?, WContract?, WDeclared).
exported procedure variant(Constant?, WContract?, WDeclared).
variant(Nm, B, C?) :- contracts # variant(Nm?, B?, C).

imported procedure compile#compile_named(Constant?).
exported procedure compile_named(Constant?).
compile_named(Nm) :- compile # compile_named(Nm?).

imported procedure compile#compile_contract(Constant?, NDeclared?).
exported procedure compile_contract(Constant?, WDeclared?).
compile_contract(Nm, D) :- ground(D?) |
    read_faults(D?, F),
    compile_read(F?, Nm?, D?).

imported procedure compile#compile_malformed(Constant?, Faults?).
procedure compile_read(Faults?, Constant?, WDeclared?).
compile_read([], Nm, D) :- unnamed(D?, D0), compile # compile_contract(Nm?, D0?).
compile_read([F|Fs], Nm, _) :- compile # compile_malformed(Nm?, [F?|Fs?]).

imported procedure compile#compile_variant(Constant?, WContract?).
exported procedure compile_variant(Constant?, WContract?).
compile_variant(Nm, B) :- compile # compile_variant(Nm?, B?).

imported procedure compile#compile_schema(Constant?, Constant?).
exported procedure compile_schema(Constant?, Constant?).
compile_schema(Nm, Sn) :- compile # compile_schema(Nm?, Sn?).

imported procedure compile#compile_schema_in(Constant?, NDeclared?, Constant?).
exported procedure compile_schema_in(Constant?, WDeclared?, Constant?).
compile_schema_in(Nm, D, Sn) :- ground(D?) |
    read_faults(D?, F),
    compile_s_read(F?, Nm?, D?, Sn?).

procedure compile_s_read(Faults?, Constant?, WDeclared?, Constant?).
compile_s_read([], Nm, D, Sn) :- unnamed(D?, D0), compile # compile_schema_in(Nm?, D0?, Sn?).
compile_s_read([F|Fs], Nm, _, _) :- compile # compile_malformed(Nm?, [F?|Fs?]).

imported procedure compile#compile_schema_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Constant?).
exported procedure compile_schema_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Constant?).
compile_schema_variant(Nm, B, Sn) :- compile # compile_schema_variant(Nm?, B?, Sn?).

imported procedure notation#notation_contract(WDeclared?).
exported procedure notation_contract(WDeclared?).
notation_contract(D) :- notation # notation_contract(D?).
